\h 2 Chronicles
\toc1 2 Chronicles
\toc2 2 Chronicles
\toc3 2 Chr.
\mt2 The second
\mt1 Sequential Account
\mt2 (2 Chronicles)
\is1 Introduction
\ip The \bk Second Chronicles\bk* account is the continuation of \bk First Chronicles\bk* account (and they're considered as just one account in the book form of the Hebrew Scripturesthe TaNaK). This document includes the account of Shelomoh (Solomon) becoming king, then the rebellion of the northern tribes against his son Rehoboam becoming king. That rebellion was led by Yeroboam (Jeroboam) and resulted in the split between the northern kingdom (called ‘Yisrael/Israel’ or sometimes ‘Efrayim/Ephraim’) and the southern king (called ‘Yehudah/Judah’ and consisting mostly of the tribes of Yehudah and Benyamin). This document then ends with the accounts of the kingdom of Yehudah (Judah) and the defeat of Yerushalem (Jerusalem) in 586 B.C.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 Shelomoh's reign \ior 1:1–9:31\ior*
\io2 a. The first years \ior 1:1-17\ior*
\io2 b. The temple construction \ior 2:1–7:10\ior*
\io2 c. The final years \ior 7:11–9:31\ior*
\io1 The rebellion of the southern tribes \ior 10:1-19\ior*
\io1 The kings of Yehudah \ior 11:1–36:12\ior*
\io1 The defeat of Yerushalem \ior 36:13-23\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 The requesting of Solomon of wisdom
\rem /s1 The reign of Solomon; King Solomon Prays for Wisdom; Solomon Asks for Wisdom; Solomon Requests Wisdom
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 3:1-15)
\p
\v 1 David's¦200723 son¦200721 Shelomoh¦200720 \add !(Solomon¦200720)\add* became established¦200719 over¦200724 his kingdom¦200726, and his god¦200728, Yahweh¦200727, was with¦200729 him and \add ≈made¦200730 him very powerful\add*.
\p
\v 2 Shelomoh¦200734 spoke¦200733 to all of Yisrael \add !(Israel¦200737)\add*, to the army commanders¦200738 of thousands¦200739 and¦200733 of hundreds¦200740, to the judges¦200741, to all of Yisrael's¦200746 leaders, including¦200740 the clan leaders.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦200750\add* Shelomoh¦200751 led the whole¦200752 assembly¦200754 to¦200756 the \add ≈worship place¦200756\add* at¦200758 Gibeon¦200758, because¦200759 the \add ≈sacred¦200763 tent¦200763\add* was there¦200761 that¦200757 Yahweh's¦200771 servant¦200769 Mosheh¦200768 \add !(Moses¦200765)\add* had¦200767 made¦200767 in¦200758 the wilderness¦200772.
\v 4 David¦200778 had¦200777 brought¦200777 God's box¦200775 uphill from¦200779 Kiriat¦200779-Yearim, \add and\add* \add *he'd\add* erected a tent¦200788 for it in¦200781 Yerushalem¦200789 \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.\x + \xo 1:4: \xt 2Sam 6:1-17; 1Ch 13:5-14; 15:25–16:1.\x*
\v 5 The bronze¦200792 altar¦200791 made¦200794 by Betsalel¦200795 (son of Uri¦200798, son of Hur¦200801) was there \add ≈in¦200803 front¦200803 of\add* Yahweh's tent¦200804, and Shelomoh¦200807 and the¦200808 assembly¦200808 \add ≈requested Yahweh's guidance there\add*.\x + \xo 1:5: \xt Exo 38:1-7.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈So¦200810\add* Shelomoh¦200811 went up to¦200813 the bronze¦200816 altar¦200815 there¦200812 at the \add ≈sacred¦200820 tent¦200820\add*, and¦200810 \add ≈in¦200817 front¦200817 of\add* Yahweh¦200818, he¦200822 sacrificed a thousand¦200825 burnt¦200824 offerings¦200824 on¦200823 it¦200823.
\p
\v 7 That¦200836 night¦200827, God¦200830 appeared¦200829 to Shelomoh¦200831 and¦200832 told him¦200833, “Ask¦200834 for what¦200835 \add you want\add* me to give¦200836 you.”
\p
\v 8 “You showed outstanding loyal¦200849 commitment to my¦200848 father¦200848 David¦200847,” Shelomoh¦200841 \add ≈replied¦200840\add* to God¦200842, “and¦200851 you've¦200844 made¦200851 me¦200851 king¦200851 in¦200852 his¦200852 place¦200852.
\v 9 Now, Yahweh¦200855 God¦200856, may your¦200858 promise¦200858 to my father¦200861 David¦200860 be confirmed, because¦200862 you¦200863 yourself have¦200864 made¦200864 me¦200864 king¦200864 over¦200865 a people¦200867 group as numerous¦200868 as the dust¦200869 on the ground.
\v 10 Give¦200875 me wisdom¦200873 and knowledge¦200874 now \add ≈as\add* I¦200878 come¦200883 and go¦200878 in¦200879 front¦200879 of these people, because¦200884 who could¦200878 make \add good\add* judgements¦200887 for this huge¦200892 people group of yours¦200890?”
\p
\v 11 “Because¦200900 that was¦200902 in your¦200915 heart¦200906,” God¦200897 \add ≈replied¦200895\add* to Shelomoh¦200899 “and you didn't ask for wealth¦200910, riches¦200911, or \add ≈fame\add*, or the¦200914 lives of¦200914 those¦200915 who¦200915 hate¦200915 you, and also¦200916 you didn't ask \add ≈for a long life¦200914\add*, but¦200895 you've¦200909 asked¦200921 for wisdom¦200925 and knowledge¦200926 for yourself¦200924 \add ≈to help you lead\add* my¦200931 people¦200931 that I've¦200933 made¦200933 you king¦200933 over,
\v 12 then I'll¦200943 give¦200943 you \add that\add* wisdom¦200936 and knowledge¦200937, \add along with\add* wealth¦200940 and riches¦200940 and fame. You'll have more than any king that preceded you or any that follows.”
\s1 Shelomoh's honour and wealth
