\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 10:26-29)
\p
\v 13 Then¦200961 Shelomoh¦200962 left the \add ≈sacred¦200969\add* tent¦200969 at¦200966 Gibeon¦200966 and¦200961 returned to Yerushalem¦200967, where he¦200971 reigned¦200971 over¦200972 Yisrael¦200974.
\rem /s1 Solomon's Military and Commercial Activity
\v 14 Then Shelomoh¦200978 built up \add his\add* chariots and horsemen, and \add ≈soon had\add* 1,400 chariots and 12,000 horsemen, which¦200994 he¦200994 stationed¦200994 in the chariot¦200996 cities¦200995 and with¦200995 \add *him\add* in Yerushalem¦201000.\x + \xo 1:14: \xt 1Ki 4:26.\x*
\v 15 The¦201018 king¦201003 made silver¦201006 and gold¦201009 in Yerushalem¦201010 as \add common\add* as stones¦201011, and he¦201014 made \add imported\add* cedar¦201013 \add timber\add* as \add common\add* as the \add local\add* sycamore¦201015 trees that¦201016 were \add ≈plentiful\add* in the lowlands.
\v 16 Shelomoh's¦201024 horses¦201022 \add ≈were imported¦201021\add* from Egypt¦201025 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* and¦201026 from the traders¦201027 in Kue \add (in modern southern Türkiye/Turkey)\add*.\x + \xo 1:16: \xt Deu 17:16.\x*
\v 17 \add ≈Egyptian¦201035 chariots¦201036 cost\add* six¦201037 hundred silver¦201039 coins and horses¦201040 cost one¦201042 hundred and fifty¦201041. (The Hittite¦201047 and Aramean kings¦201048 were able to get them¦201051 \add ≈for the¦201048 same price\add*.)
\c 2
\s1 Preparations for temple construction
\rem /s1 Preparations for Building the Temple
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 5:1-18)
\p
\v 1 Then Shelomoh¦201065 \add ≈decided to build a temple to honour\add* Yahweh, as well as a \add ≈palace for himself\add*,
\v 2 \add ≈so he¦201084 conscripted\add* seventy thousand men as porters, eighty thousand as stone-cutters in the hillside quarries, and 3,600 supervisors.
\rem /s1 Alliance with Huram of Tyre
\p
\v 3 Shelomoh \add ≈contacted\add* King Huram in Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add*, saying, “\add ≈In\add* my¦201119 father David's \add ≈time\add*, you sent cedar \add timber\add* to him¦201123 so he could build¦201113 himself a palace to live in.
\v 4 Listen, I'm¦201147 building¦201148 a \add ≈temple to honour\add* my god¦201153 Yahweh, to consecrate to him. There we'll burn spiced incense for him, plus¦201144 we'll have the regular \add bread\add* display, and burnt offerings in the morning and in the evening, on rest days and on the new moons, and at Yahweh our¦201153 god's¦201153 \add ≈other\add* appointed times. \add ≈Yisrael is required to do\add* this forever.
\v 5 \add ≈We want to¦201163 build¦201163 an impressive building¦201163, because¦201167 our god is more powerful\add* than all \add the other\add* gods.
\v 6 \add ≈But¦201187\add* who could \add ≈stay strong enough\add* to build a house for him, since the \add ≈sky\add* and the heavens of the heavens can't contain him? And who am I that I could build a house for him—\add ≈maybe I'm good enough to burn incense for him\add*?\x + \xo 2:6: \xt 1Ki 8:27; 2Ch 6:18.\x*
\v 7 \add ≈So then,\add* send¦201218 me a skilled man who can work in gold, and in silver, and in bronze, and in iron, and with purple, red, and blue \add threads\add*, and who knows how to¦201232 engrave. \add He'll work\add* with the¦201233 skilled \add craftsmen\add* who my¦201236 father David appointed and who are with me \add here\add* in Yerushalem and across Yehudah.
\v 8 \add ≈Also,\add* send me cedar, cypress, and algum timber from \add there in\add* Lebanon, because¦201246 I¦201250 myself know that¦201248 your servants know how to cut the trees from Lebanon's \add forests\add*. And listen, my servants will \add ≈help\add* your servants
\v 9 so they can supply me with plenty of¦201259 timber¦201261, because the¦201261 temple I'm¦201262 building will be large and beautiful.
\v 10 I'll pay your wood-cutters three thousand tonnes of ground wheat, and the same amount of barley, and four hundred thousand litres of wine, and the same amount of \add olive\add* oil.
\p
\v 11 King Huram¦201306 of¦201309 Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add* wrote back to¦201321 \add King\add* Shelomoh, “Yahweh¦201308 has appointed you as king¦201322 over his people because he loves them.
\v 12 Blessed be Yisrael's god Yahweh who made the heavens and the earth, who's¦201342 given King David a wise¦201341 son with insight and understanding¦201343, who'll build a temple for Yahweh and a palace for his kingdom.
\p
\v 13 “I'll¦201390 send Huram-Avi to you—he's a skilled¦201386 craftsman.
\v 14 \add ≈His mother's\add* from the \add ≈tribe\add* of Dan, and his father's from Tsor. He knows how to work in gold and silver, in bronze and iron, in stone and in timber, with purple and blue \add threads\add*, with fine \add white\add* linen and with crimson \add thread\add*, and \add ≈do any kind of\add* engraving. \add ≈He can follow any pattern\add* that's given to him¦201401 by your \add ≈designers, and the designers\add* of my master¦201400, David, your father.
\v 15 \add So then go ahead\add* and send the¦201410 wheat, barley, \add olive\add* oil, and wine that \add *you¦201422\add* promised to send to \add *us\add*,
\v 16 then we'll cut the trees you need from Lebanon and raft them to Yafo by sea. \add ≈The responsibility of¦201436 getting them up the hills to Yerushalem will be yours\add*.
\s1 Temple construction begins
