\r (1 Kgs 6:1-38)
\p
\v 17 Shelomoh had all the¦201470 foreign men living in¦201461 Yisrael counted¦201461 (similar to what his father David had done), and¦201453 it¦201453 came to 153,600.
\v 18 He conscripted seventy thousand as porters, eighty thousand as stone-cutters, and 3,600 as supervisors to keep the others working.
\c 3
\rem /s1 Solomon Builds the Temple
\p
\v 1 Then¦201472 Shelomoh¦201473 began¦201472 to build¦201474 Yahweh's¦201479 temple on¦201480 Mt¦201481. Moriyah¦201482 in¦201480 Yerushalem¦201480, where \add @Yahweh\add* had appeared¦201484 to his¦201486 father¦201486 David. It was at¦201480 Ornan¦201492 the Yevusite's¦201493 threshing¦201491 floor¦201491 where David \add ≈had planned for it\add*,\x + \xo 3:1: \xt Gen 22:22.\x*
\v 2 and¦201495 they began¦201495 the construction in early-May of the fourth year¦201500 of Shelomoh's reign¦201502.\f + \fr 3:2 \ft Probably in 966 B.C.\f*
\v 3 \add ≈The temple foundation¦201505 was twenty-seven¦201520 metres long and¦201518 nine metres wide\add*,
\v 4 and¦201522 the nine metre long¦201527 front¦201526 entrance porch¦201522 was nine metres¦201534 high.\f + \fr 3:4 \ft Most modern translations assume that the Hebrew ‘fifty-five metres high’ is an error.\f* \add @Shelomoh\add* overlaid¦201539 the inside¦201540 \add walls\add* with pure¦201542 gold¦201541.
\v 5 For the \add ≈main building\add*, he overlaid it first with cypress¦201550 planking, then with pure gold¦201552, then \add ≈carved\add* palm¦201556 trees¦201556 and¦201544 chains¦201557 \add along the walls\add*.
\v 6 The gold \add they used\add* came from Parvaim¦201568.\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Probably somewhere south of Yisrael in the Arabian peninsula, but possibly to the east.\f* \add ≈The main building\add* was \add also\add* overlaid¦201559 with valuable gemstones.
\v 7 He¦201570 overlaid¦201570 the temple beams¦201574, thresholds¦201575, walls, and doors¦201577 with gold¦201578, and he¦201579 engraved¦201579 winged creatures on¦201581 the walls.
\p
\v 8 Then he¦201586 made¦201586 the \add ≈most sacred¦201591 room¦201591\add* \add inside\add* the temple. It was nine metres¦201600 long \add (the full width of the temple)\add* and the same width. He¦201605 overlaid¦201605 it¦201605 with thirty kilograms of pure¦201591 gold¦201606 \add (beaten into thin sheets)\add*.\x + \xo 3:8: \xt Exo 26:33-34.\x*
\v 9 Each gold nail weighed¦201612 half a kilogram, and¦201612 he also overlaid¦201618 the upper¦201617 rooms¦201617 with gold.
\p
\v 10 He¦201621 cast \add molten metal\add* into two¦201627 winged creatures in¦201622 the \add ≈most sacred¦201624 room¦201624\add* and¦201630 overlaid¦201630 them¦201631 with gold¦201632.\x + \xo 3:10-13: \xt Exo 25:18-20.\x*
\v 11 Each of the creatures had two wings, each 2.3 metres¦201637 long. One¦201640 of the wings reached the temple wall¦201644, and¦201646 the other wing¦201651 was¦201650 stretched out to¦201651 touch¦201650 the other creature's wingtip,
\v 12 and¦201655 \add ≈the same for its companion\add*,
\v 13 \add so\add* the total span of the two winged creatures was nine metres¦201676. They¦201678 \add were made\add* standing¦201679 on¦201680 their feet¦201682, and¦201683 \add placed\add* with their faces¦201683 towards¦201684 \add the opening into\add* the main hall.
\v 14 The \add ≈curtain¦201690\add* \add separating the two rooms\add* was made¦201687 from fine-linen with blue, purple¦201692, and red thread, and with winged creatures \add embroidered\add* onto it.\x + \xo 3:14: \xt Exo 26:31.\x*
\s1 The two bronze pillars
\rem /s1 The Two Bronze Columns
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 7:15-22)
\p
\v 15 For the front¦201701 of the temple he made¦201700 two sixteen metre tall pillars¦201703, which¦201710 each had a ‘capital¦201709’ topping that¦201710 was another two metres¦201705 high.
\v 16 \add Ornamental\add* chains were made¦201727 for the inner¦201721 sanctuary¦201721 and to go around the tops of¦201725 the pillars¦201726, and there were one¦201729 hundred¦201729 pomegranate¦201728 \add models\add* hanging on¦201721 the chains.
\v 17 There was one pillar¦201736 on¦201737 each side of the \add east-facing\add* entrance—the lefthand one was named Yakin¦201750 and¦201733 the righthand¦201748 one was named Boaz¦201753.
\c 4
\s1 The temple equipment
\rem /s1 Furnishings for the Temple; Equipment for the Temple; Furnishings of the Temple; The Temple's Furnishings
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 7:23-51)
\p
\v 1 Then he¦201756 made¦201756 a \add ≈square\add* bronze¦201758 altar¦201757, nine metres¦201766 on each side and 4.5m high¦201767,\x + \xo 4:1: \xt Exo 27:1-2.\x*
\v 2 and he¦201770 made¦201770 the large round metal¦201774 \add water tank\add* (\add called\add* ‘The Sea’), which was 4.5m in diameter and over two metres¦201776 high¦201786.
\v 3 \add ≈Below the outer rim were two¦201810 rows¦201811 of small ornamental bulls¦201795 spaced 45cm apart, which were part of the same casting\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈Supporting ‘The¦201837 Sea¦201837’ were¦201843 twelve large cast bulls—facing outwards, with three facing each¦201840 of¦201842 the¦201843 four compass points\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈The sides of the tank were eight centimeters thick¦201845. The tank's brim was fashioned¦201848 like¦201848 the brim of a cup¦201851, resembling a lily¦201853 blossom¦201852\add*. \add @The tank\add* held¦201854 sixty-six thousand¦201857 litres of water.
\v 6 Then he made¦201861 ten¦201863 washbasins, placing five on¦201876 \add ≈each side for the priests to rinse¦201875 the burnt¦201874 offerings¦201874 in\add*. The priests used ‘The Sea¦201877’ to wash¦201878 in.\x + \xo 4:6: \xt Exo 30:17-21.\x*
\p
\v 7 He¦201883 made¦201883 the ten¦201888 gold¦201887 lampstands¦201886 as per their¦201889 design, and¦201890 placed them in¦201891 the temple¦201891 \add ≈with¦201891 five¦201894 on¦201891 each side\add*.\x + \xo 4:7: \xt Exo 25:31-40.\x*
\v 8 He¦201898 made ten¦201900 tables¦201899 and¦201901 \add also\add* placed¦201901 them¦201901 in¦201902 the¦201904 temple¦201902 \add ≈with¦201902 five¦201905 on¦201902 each side\add*, plus¦201898 he¦201907 made a hundred¦201910 gold¦201909 basins.\x + \xo 4:8: \xt Exo 25:23-30.\x*
\p
\v 9 He¦201912 made¦201912 the courtyard for the priests¦201914, as well as the large¦201916 courtyard with its doors overlaid¦201920 with bronze¦201921,
\v 10 and¦201923 he¦201926 placed ‘The Sea¦201925’ in¦201930 the¦201931 southeast¦201931 corner.
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Huram¦201934 made¦201933 the tubs and shovels¦201940 \add (for the ashes from the altar)\add* and \add other small\add* bowls¦201943.
\p \add ≈So¦201933\add* Huram finished¦201945 the¦201937 work¦201951 for God's temple that¦201952 King¦201954 Shelomoh¦201955 had assigned to¦201954 him:
\v 12 the two pillars, the \add ≈bowl-shaped\add* capitals on¦201963 top¦201965 of each pillar¦201966, the two \add ≈sets of latticework¦201968\add* to¦201970 cover¦201970 those two capitals' bowls¦201974,
\v 13 and¦201982 the four¦201985 hundred¦201986 pomegranates for¦201987 the latticework¦201988—two rows¦201990 of pomegranates to¦201994 cover¦201994 each of the two bowls¦201998 of the capitals¦201999 that¦202000 \add ≈decorated the tops\add* of the pillars¦202004.
\v 14 He also made the washbasins and¦202010 their stands¦202016,
\v 15 ‘The¦202020 Sea¦202020’ and¦202022 the¦202024 twelve bulls¦202024 that hold it¦202028 up,
\v 16 and the tubs and shovels¦202035, the forks¦202038, and other utensils¦202043.
\p Those were all¦202041 items made of polished¦202052 bronze¦202051 that Huram¦202045-Abi¦202046 made for King¦202047 Shelomoh¦202048 for Yahweh's¦202050 temple.
\p
\v 17 The king¦202057 had them¦202056 cast in¦202058 the clay between¦202060 Sukkot¦202061 and¦202062 Tseredah¦202063 \add down\add* by the Yordan¦202055 River.
\v 18 Shelomoh¦202066 had \add ≈so many items made¦202065 that they didn't¦202074 even try to weigh¦202076 all\add* the bronze¦202077.
\p
\v 19 Shelomoh¦202081 had all¦202083 the items for God's¦202088 temple made¦202080, including¦202080 the gold¦202091 altar¦202090 and the tables¦202094 \add ≈for displaying the sacred bread¦202096\add*,
\v 20 the pure¦202108 gold¦202108 lampstands¦202101 and¦202099 their lamps¦202102 for the inner¦202106 sanctuary¦202106 according¦202104 to¦202105 their designs,
\v 21 the pure gold flower¦202110 \add ornaments\add*, lamps¦202111, tongs¦202112,
\v 22 the pure¦202128 gold lamp trimmers, the basins¦202119 and spoons, and the fire pans. Also¦202118 the temple entrance¦202124, its¦202126 inner¦202127 doors into the very sacred¦202128 room¦202128, and the \add outer\add* temple doors were \add all\add* gold.
\c 5
\rem /s1 The Ark Brought to the Temple
\p
\v 1 \add ≈After\add* all the work¦202138 which¦202139 Shelomoh did¦202141 for¦202143 Yahweh's¦202144 temple was completed¦202135, Shelomoh brought¦202146 in his father¦202153 David's¦202152 sacred¦202150 things¦202150. He put¦202165 the gold¦202159 and silver¦202156, and all the \add other\add* items, in the temple treasuries¦202166.\x + \xo 5:1: \xt 2Sam 8:11; 1Ch 18:11.\x*
\s1 Bringing the sacred box into the temple
\rem /s1 The Ark Brought into the Temple; The Covenant Box Is Brought to the Temple; The Ark Brought to the Temple
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 8:1-9)
\p
\v 2 Then¦202171 Shelomoh¦202173 assembled¦202172 the Israeli elders¦202176, and¦202178 all¦202180 the heads of the tribes¦202183, the Israeli \add ≈clan leaders¦202184\add*, in Yerushalem¦202190, to bring¦202191 the box¦202194 \add ≈containing\add* Yahweh's¦202197 agreement¦202195 up \add the hill\add* from¦202198 the city¦202198 of David¦202199, that¦202200 is¦202201, Tsiyyon¦202201 \add !(Zion)\add*.\x + \xo 5:2: \xt 2Sam 6:12-15; 1Ch 15:25-28.\x*
\v 3 \add ≈So¦202203 in¦202211 October¦202210,\add* all those Israeli¦202209 leaders gathered to¦202204 be with¦202211 the king¦202206 for a feast,
\v 4 and¦202220 once \add ≈everyone¦202217 was there\add*, the Levites¦202221 lifted¦202220 up the \add sacred\add* box¦202224
\v 5 and carried it up \add towards the temple\add*. The priests¦202244 (who are also Levites¦202245) carried it, along with¦202241 the \add sacred\add* tent and everything that¦202240 had been in¦202241 it.
\v 6 Then¦202247 King¦202247 Shelomoh¦202248, and all¦202249 the assembled¦202253 Israelis¦202251 with him¦202254, gathered¦202253 in¦202255 front¦202255 of¦202255 the box¦202256, sacrificing¦202257 sheep¦202258 and cattle¦202259 which¦202260 were too many to count¦202263.
\v 7 The priests¦202269 then¦202268 took the box¦202272 \add ≈containing\add* Yahweh's¦202275 agreement¦202273 in to its¦202278 place¦202286 in the house's¦202282 inner¦202281 room¦202278 (the \add ≈holiest place\add*)—to under¦202289 the winged creatures,
\v 8 whose outstretched wings¦202296 would now be over the \add sacred\add* box¦202300 and¦202293 even over the top of¦202308 its¦202308 carrying poles¦202308.
\v 9 \add ≈Those long¦202311 poles¦202312 stuck out and could be seen from the front¦202321 of that¦202331 inner¦202322 room, but¦202311 couldn't be seen from the main room\add*, and they're still there¦202328 to¦202325 this¦202331 day¦202330.
\v 10 There¦202333 was¦202333 nothing in the box¦202334 except the two¦202336 \add stone\add* tablets¦202337 that Mosheh¦202341 \add !(Moses¦202341)\add* had \add ≈put¦202340 in\add* at¦202334 Horev¦202342 \add !(Mt¦202342. Sinai¦202342)\add*, which¦202338 \add represented the agreement that\add* Yahweh¦202345 \add ≈had made¦202344 with¦202334 the Israelis¦202348 after\add* they'd left¦202350 Egypt¦202351 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*.\x + \xo 5:10: \xt Deu 10:5.\x*
\s1 Yahweh's splendour
\rem /s1 The Glory of the Lord
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Then the priests left¦202355 the holy¦202359 place¦202359 in¦202355 the temple. All¦202361 the priests who¦202364 were there consecrated¦202365 themselves¦202365 to do the priestly duties, irrespective of which division¦202368 they were part of\add*.
\v 12 All the Levites¦202370 who were singers¦202371 (Asaf¦202373, Heyman¦202374, Yedutun¦202375, and their sons¦202376 and their brothers) stood¦202383 on¦202380 the east side of the altar¦202385. \add ≡They\add* were dressed in¦202380 fine linen¦202379, and had cymbals¦202380, and harps¦202381 and lyres¦202382, along with¦202380 120 priests¦202387 playing trumpets¦202390.
\v 13 The trumpeters¦202396 and singers¦202398 performed together to praise and thank¦202404 Yahweh, with the trumpets¦202408 and cymbals¦202409 on¦202408 the highlights of¦202410 the song¦202411 to praise Yahweh:\x + \xo 5:13: \xt 1Ch 16:34; 2Ch 7:3; Ezr 3:11; Psa 100:5; 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; Jer 33:11.\x*
\q1 “\add Yahweh\add* is good¦202415 to¦202413 us,
\q1 because¦202414 his¦202418 loyal¦202418 commitment continues forever¦202417.”
\p Then¦202394 Yahweh's¦202405 temple filled with a cloud¦202421,
\v 14 and the priests¦202428 weren't able¦202427 to stay on their feet and continue ministering¦202430, because¦202433 Yahweh's¦202438 brilliance had filled¦202435 the temple.
\c 6
\s1 Shelomoh's blessing
\rem /s1 Solomon's Address to the People; Dedication of the Temple; Solomon Blesses the People
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 8:12-21)
\p
\v 1 Then¦202445 Shelomoh¦202447 \add ≈prayed\add*, “\add ≈Yahweh¦202448, you said that you\add* would live in¦202451 a dark cloud,
\v 2 \add ≈but¦202453\add* I've¦202454 built¦202454 a \add ≈beautiful\add* residence for you—a place¦202459 for you to¦202460 live in¦202460 forever¦202461.”
\p
\v 3 \add ≈Then¦202463, while all the people stood¦202478\add* \add there\add*, Shelomoh turned¦202463 toward them and¦202463 \add ≈spoke a blessing¦202468 over\add* them,
\v 4 saying¦202480, “Yahweh¦202482, Yisrael¦202484's god¦202483, is blessed¦202481, who¦202485 spoke¦202486 \add ≈physically\add* to my¦202490 father¦202490 David¦202489, and¦202491 \add ≈then caused it¦202480 to actually happen\add*, when he said¦202480 \add back then\add*,\x + \xo 6:4-9: \xt 2Sam 7:1-13; 1Ch 17:1-12.\x*
\v 5 ‘When¦202498 I brought¦202499 my people out of Egypt¦202504, I hadn't chosen a city¦202508 from¦202509 all¦202509 of Yisrael¦202511's tribes¦202510 as a place to build¦202512 a house¦202513 so my name¦202515 could be there¦202516. Nor had I chosen a man¦202520 to be leader¦202522 over¦202523 my people, Yisrael¦202511,
\v 6 \add ≈but¦202528\add* \add now\add* I've chosen Yerushalem¦202529 \add !(Jerusalem¦202529)\add* \add ≈to be my place of residence\add*, and¦202533 I've chosen \add you\add*, David¦202534, to be over¦202536 my people¦202538, Yisrael¦202539.’
\p
\v 7 “My¦202546 father¦202546 David¦202545 wanted to¦202547 build¦202547 a temple for¦202549 Yisrael's¦202552 god¦202551 Yahweh¦202550,
\v 8 \add ≈but¦202554\add* Yahweh¦202555 told \add *him\add*, ‘\add ≈It's¦202558 good that you¦202569 wanted to build¦202566 a house¦202567 to honour me\add*,
\v 9 \add ≈but\add* you won't¦202578 be the one to build it. It'll be your¦202584 own \add ≈biological\add* son¦202582 who'll build the temple to honour my¦202589 \add ≈reputation¦202589\add*.’
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈Now\add* Yahweh has¦202591 fulfilled¦202591 what he said, and I'm here sitting¦202602 on Yisrael's throne¦202606 instead of my father¦202601 David¦202600, just¦202608 as¦202608 Yahweh said, and I've¦202598 had this temple built¦202611 to honour Yisrael's god¦202615 Yahweh.
\v 11 I've¦202618 placed the \add sacred\add* box in there—\add @the box\add* that¦202628 contains the agreement¦202626 Yahweh¦202627 made¦202629 with Yisrael's¦202633 descendants.”
\s1 Shelomoh's prayer
\rem /s1 Solomon's Prayer; Solomon's Prayer of Dedication
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 8:22-53)
\p
\v 12 Then¦202635 \add @Shelomoh¦202643\add* stood¦202635 in front of the altar¦202637 to Yahweh¦202638 in front of all¦202640 the assembled¦202642 Israelis¦202642, and¦202644 spread¦202644 out¦202644 his¦202645 hands¦202645,
\v 13 because¦202647 \add *he'd¦202650\add* made¦202649 a bronze¦202652 platform and had¦202653 it placed in the centre of the courtyard¦202655. The square platform was just over two metres¦202657 on each¦202672 side, and stood just over a metre off the ground. \add ≈Firstly\add* he stood on it, then he knelt¦202667 down¦202667 in front¦202671 of all¦202672 the assembled¦202674 Israelis¦202674 and spread¦202676 his hands¦202677 out to¦202678 the \add #sky\add*
\v 14 and said¦202680, “Yahweh¦202681, Yisrael¦202683's god¦202682, there¦202684 isn't¦202684 any god like¦202686 you in¦202688 the heavens¦202688 or on¦202688 the earth¦202689—one who keeps¦202690 his agreement¦202691 and \add shows\add* loyal¦202692 commitment to your servants¦202693 who are walking¦202694 \add ≈with¦202688 total¦202696 integrity as you watch them\add*.
\v 15 \add ≈Everything you verbally told my¦202704 father¦202704 David¦202703 that¦202706 you'd do, you've¦202701 used your power to¦202709 make it¦202709 all happen, including¦202710 this¦202715 today\add*.
\v 16 And now¦202717, Yahweh¦202718, Yisrael's god¦202720, keep¦202722 \add another promise you made\add* to¦202723 your servant¦202723 David¦202725 my father¦202726, when you told him¦202730, ‘There'll \add ≈always be¦202734 one of your descendants¦202747 sitting¦202738 on¦202752 Yisrael's throne¦202741, as long as they¦202746 obey my instructions just¦202753 like you have¦202754\add*.’\x + \xo 6:16: \xt 1Ki 2:4.\x*
\v 17 \add ≈So¦202757\add* now¦202757, Yahweh¦202758, Yisrael¦202760's god¦202759, may what you¦202764 said to your¦202765 servant¦202765, to David¦202766, be confirmed.
\p
\v 18 “But¦202780 will¦202770 God¦202771 really¦202769 live with¦202772 humans¦202774 \add here\add* on the earth¦202777? Wow¦202778, the skies¦202780 and¦202780 the heavens of¦202780 the heavens can't¦202782 contain¦202783 you¦202783—how much less this¦202788 house¦202787 that¦202789 I've¦202790 built¦202790.\x + \xo 6:18: \xt 2Ch 2:6.\x*
\v 19 \add ≈Nevertheless\add* Yahweh¦202800 my god¦202801, listen¦202802 to¦202793 your¦202812 servant's¦202796 prayer¦202795 and request \add ≈and take notice\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈Watch over this building\add* where¦202826 you said¦202827 \add ≈you'd be present\add*, and¦202822 hear \add &my\add* prayers¦202834 when your servant¦202837 prays¦202836 towards this place.\x + \xo 6:20: \xt Deu 12:11.\x*
\v 21 Listen \add ≈to¦202844 what your servant¦202847 and your Israeli people¦202848 are requesting\add* when they¦202851 pray¦202851 towards this¦202855 place¦202858. Listen from¦202860 where you live in the¦202862 heavens¦202862, and hear¦202863 and forgive¦202864.
\p
\v 22 “If someone¦202869 \add is accused of\add* wronging their neighbour¦202870, and is forced to make a sworn statement in front¦202878 of your¦202879 altar¦202879 in this¦202881 temple,
\v 23 then¦202883 \add ≈listen¦202885\add* from¦202886 the heavens¦202888 and \add ≈decide who's telling the truth\add*. \add ≈Then¦202883 punish the guilty¦202895 party as they deserve, and do good to the other side as a reward¦202901 for their innocence\add*.
\p
\v 24 “And¦202906 if¦202906 your Israeli¦202910 people¦202909 are \add ≈defeated¦202908 by their enemies because¦202913 they've disobeyed\add* you, but¦202906 they return¦202917 \add to you\add* and confess¦202918, and pray¦202922, and in¦202925 this place they \add ≈request¦202923 your\add* favour¦202923,
\v 25 then¦202928 listen¦202929 to them from¦202930 the¦202932 heavens¦202932 and forgive¦202933 your Israeli¦202936 people's¦202935 disobedience, and bring¦202937 them back¦202937 to this land that¦202941 you¦202943 gave¦202943 to their¦202945 ancestors¦202945 and to them.
\p
\v 26 “When¦202948 \add ≈the¦202949 clouds hold back\add* and give no rain¦202953 because \add ≈your Israeli people have disobeyed\add* you, but¦202950 then they pray¦202958 towards this place¦202961 and \add ≈acknowledge you\add* and turn¦202968 away from¦202967 their¦202967 disobedience because you've punished them¦202970,
\v 27 then¦202972 listen¦202974 to them from the heavens¦202975 and forgive¦202976 the \add ≈disobedience\add* of¦202977 your servants¦202978 and your Israeli people. Teach them the \add ≈right way¦202985 to live their lives\add*, and give¦202991 rain¦202992 to your land¦202995 which¦202996 you¦202998 gave¦202998 your people as a \add ≈permanent inheritance¦203000\add*.
\p
\v 28 “If this land¦203023 \add suffers\add* from famine¦203003, or if there's blight¦203012 or mildew¦203013, or locusts¦203014 or grasshoppers, \add ≈deadly diseases\add* or sickness¦203030, or if an enemy \add army\add* surrounds them,
\v 29 then if any¦203040 person, or all¦203043 your¦203044 Israeli¦203045 people¦203044, stretch¦203051 out their hands¦203052 towards this temple with their prayers¦203034 and requests because they¦203047 each¦203043 acknowledge their individual pain¦203050 and suffering,
\v 30 then¦203058 listen¦203059 to them from where you live there in the heavens¦203062, and¦203058 forgive¦203065 them. \add ≈Reward\add* each¦203068 person¦203067 according¦203068 to their behaviour, because¦203076 you know \add ≈people's motives\add*—only you know \add ≈what's in people's minds\add*.
\v 31 \add Do that\add* so they'll¦203095 respect you and \add ≈live how you want them to\add*, as they live in¦203089 \add ≈this country\add* that you gave¦203102 to our¦203103 ancestors¦203103.
\p
\v 32 “Also¦203106, any foreigners¦203109 who don't¦203111 belong to your Israeli¦203113 people¦203112, who come¦203115 to this land¦203117 because they've \add ≈heard that¦203131 you're very great¦203121 and powerful\add*, if they turn toward this temple and pray¦203127,
\v 33 then¦203133 listen¦203134 to them \add as well\add* from where you live there in the heavens¦203137. Do¦203140 whatever that foreigner¦203146 requests from you, so¦203147 that all¦203149 the people groups in the world will learn about¦203138 your reputation¦203155, and \add ≈honour and obey\add* you like¦203158 your Israeli¦203159 people do¦203140, and know¦203160 that this temple that I've¦203170 built¦203170 is called¦203164 by your name¦203163.
\p
\v 34 “When you send¦203182 your people¦203175 off to battle¦203176 their¦203179 enemies¦203179, and they¦203183 pray¦203183 towards this city¦203186 that you've¦203189 chosen¦203189 and this temple that I've¦203194 had built¦203194 \add to honour\add* your name¦203195,
\v 35 then¦203197 listen¦203197 from¦203198 the¦203200 heavens¦203200 to their prayer¦203203 and their requests, and \add ≈uphold¦203207 their cause¦203208\add*.
\p
\v 36 “When they¦203211 disobey you (and there's¦203215 no one who¦203217 doesn't), and you're angry¦203221 with¦203222 them and allow an enemy¦203225 \add ≈to get the¦203224 upper hand\add*, and their¦203227 captors¦203227 take¦203226 them to a distant¦203231 or¦203232 nearby land¦203230 as captives¦203227,
\v 37 and then¦203235 in that land¦203248 where¦203240 they're captives¦203241, they turn and admit their wickedness¦203253 and their disobedience, and request¦203246 your favour¦203246,
\v 38 and they¦203255 turn to you with total¦203257 sincerity in that other country, and pray¦203269 towards the land¦203271 that you gave¦203273 their¦203274 ancestors¦203274, and the city¦203275 that you chose¦203277, and toward the temple that I've¦203281 built¦203281 \add to honour\add* your¦203282 name¦203282,
\v 39 then¦203284 listen¦203284 from where you live in the heavens¦203288 to their prayer¦203293 and their requests, and \add ≈uphold¦203297 their cause¦203298\add* and forgive¦203299 your people¦203300 who've \add ≈disobeyed\add* you.
\p
\v 40 “Now¦203307 my god¦203307, please¦203310 let¦203308 your eyes¦203311 be open¦203312 and¦203313 your ears¦203313 attentive¦203314 to¦203315 prayers¦203315 \add offered towards\add* this¦203317 place¦203316.
\p
\v 41 “\add ≈So\add* now¦203320 Yahweh God, along with¦203335 the \add sacred\add* box¦203326 \add ≈representing\add* your strength¦203327, come and enter your place¦203324 for resting¦203324. Yahweh God, may your priests¦203328 be¦203331 dressed in¦203335 \add your\add* rescue¦203332, and your faithful¦203333 ones enjoy \add your\add* goodness¦203335.\x + \xo 6:41-42: \xt Psa 132:8-10.\x*
\v 42 Yahweh¦203337 God¦203338, don't¦203339 \add ≈ignore\add* those who you've chosen. Remember¦203344 your servant¦203347 David's¦203346 loyal¦203345 commitment.”
\c 7
\s1 The temple dedication
\rem /s1 The Dedication of the Temple; Solomon Dedicates the Temple
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 8:62-66)
\p
\v 1 When¦203351 Shelomoh¦203351 \add !(Solomon¦203351)\add* finished¦203350 praying¦203352, fire¦203353 came¦203354 down¦203354 from¦203355 the skies¦203355 and consumed the burnt¦203357 offering¦203357 and the sacrifices¦203358, and Yahweh's¦203360 \add ≈brilliant light\add* filled¦203361 the temple.\x + \xo 7:1: \xt Lev 9:23-24.\x*
\v 2 The¦203368 priests¦203368 weren't able¦203367 to¦203369 go¦203369 into¦203370 Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add* because¦203374 of Yahweh's \add ≈brilliant light\add*,
\v 3 and when all¦203385 the \add ≈Israelis¦203387\add* saw the fire¦203391 come¦203390 down and saw the \add ≈bright light\add* above the \add ≈temple\add*, they¦203397 fell \add to their knees with\add* their faces bowed¦203397 down low to the stone pavement¦203402, and worshipped¦203403 and thanked¦203404 Yahweh¦203393, saying, “He's¦203407 certainly good¦203407—his loyal¦203410 commitment really will \add continue\add* forever¦203409.”\x + \xo 7:3: \xt 1Ch 16:34; 2Ch 5:13; Ezr 3:11; Psa 100:5; 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; Jer 33:11.\x*
\p
\v 4 Then¦203412 the king¦203412 and¦203413 all¦203413 the people¦203415 offered sacrifices¦203416 to¦203418 Yahweh¦203419—
\v 5 King¦203423 Shelomoh¦203424 sacrificed¦203422 twenty-two¦203429 thousand cattle¦203428 and one¦203433 hundred¦203433 and twenty thousand sheep¦203432, and \add so\add* the king¦203441 and all¦203442 the people¦203444 dedicated¦203436 God's¦203440 \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 6 The¦203446 priests were standing¦203450 in their positions, as well as the Levites¦203451 with¦203452 the instruments¦203452 King¦203459 David had¦203457 made¦203457 to give¦203460 thanks¦203460 to Yahweh. When¦203446 \add ≈they assisted\add* David in praising¦203466 \add Yahweh\add*, \add they would sing\add*, “\add ≈Yes,\add* his¦203465 loyal¦203465 commitment \add continues\add* forever¦203464,” and¦203446 the priests \add ≈would blow¦203470 their trumpets¦203470\add* in front¦203472 of them¦203472 as all¦203473 the \add ≈Israelis¦203475\add* stood \add there\add*.
\p
\v 7 Then¦203504 Shelomoh¦203480 consecrated¦203479 the middle¦203483 of the courtyard¦203484 \add ≈in¦203486 front¦203486\add* of Yahweh's¦203489 \add ≈temple building\add* so he could offer¦203492 burnt offerings and the fat of the peace¦203497 offerings there¦203493, because¦203490 the bronze¦203501 altar¦203500 that¦203485 \add *he'd\add* made¦203503 wasn't able¦203506 to¦203507 \add ≈handle\add* the \add large number of\add* burnt offerings and grain¦203513 offerings, and the fats¦203516.
\p
\v 8 Then¦203518 Shelomoh¦203519 and¦203527 all of Yisrael¦203529 feasted for the \add next\add* seven¦203525 days¦203526—the huge¦203532 gathering spread from Levo¦203534-Hamat¦203535 \add in the far north\add*, all the way to¦203536 the Egyptian¦203539 riverbed¦203538 \add in the far south\add*.
\v 9 On the eighth¦203543 day¦203542, they \add ≈had¦203549 a solemn service\add*, because¦203545 they'd observed¦203549 seven days of celebration for the altar¦203548 \add ?≈with seven days of feasting\add*.
\v 10 \add ≈Finally, after some three¦203558 weeks,\add* \add @Shelomoh\add* sent¦203561 the people \add ≈home\add*—they were cheery and \add ≈encouraged\add* because of¦203567 the goodness¦203571 Yahweh¦203574 had¦203573 \add ≈displayed to\add* David¦203575 and Shelomoh, and to his Israeli people.
\s1 Yahweh appears to Shelomoh again
\rem /s1 The Lord Appears to Solomon; The Lord's Response to Solomon; God Appears to Solomon Again
\s4 Full kingdom
\rem /r (1 Kings 9.1-9)
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦203580\add* Shelomoh¦203581 finished¦203580 Yahweh's¦203585 \add ≈temple\add* and¦203580 the king's¦203589 \add ≈palace¦203602\add*—he'd succeeded¦203603 in¦203602 \add ≈implementing everything¦203591 he'd envisaged\add*.
\rem /s1 God's Second Appearance to Solomon
\v 12 \add ≈One\add* night¦203611, Yahweh¦203607 appeared¦203606 to Shelomoh¦203610 in¦203611 a dream and told him¦203613, “I've heard¦203614 your¦203617 prayer¦203617, and I've chosen¦203618 this \add ≈temple to be the place¦203619 where my people will offer sacrifices¦203623\add* \add to me\add*.
\v 13 If I restrain the skies¦203627 \add ≈so\add* there's no rain¦203631, or if I command¦203634 locusts to devour¦203638 the land¦203639, or if I send¦203642 disease among¦203644 my¦203644 people¦203644,
\v 14 \add ≈then if\add* my people¦203647 \add ≈who are known by my name¦203651\add* humble¦203646 themselves¦203646 and pray¦203653, and \add ≈request¦203654 my help\add* and turn¦203656 away from their evil customs¦203657, then I myself will¦203660 hear¦203660 \add >them\add* from the¦203663 heavens¦203663, and I'll¦203660 forgive¦203664 their sin¦203665 and heal¦203666 their land¦203669.
\v 15 My¦203672 eyes¦203672 will be open¦203674 and¦203675 my¦203675 ears¦203675 will be attentive¦203676 to¦203677 prayers¦203677 \add ≈offered towards\add* this¦203679 place¦203678,
\v 16 as I've¦203682 chosen¦203682 and¦203681 consecrated¦203683 this¦203687 \add ≈temple to¦203688 be associated with my¦203690 name¦203690 forever¦203694—I'll¦203683 be permanently present there¦203698\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈Also¦203703, if¦203704 you'll¦203706 obey\add* me like your¦203711 father¦203711 David¦203710 did, and do¦203712 everything that¦203714 I've¦203715 instructed¦203715 you, and keep my¦203716 rules and regulations¦203716,
\v 18 then¦203720 \add ≈I'll¦203727 ensure that your descendants rule your kingdom¦203723\add*, just¦203724 as¦203724 I \add ≈promised\add* your father¦203727 David¦203726 when I said¦203728, ‘\add ≈You won't¦203729 fail to¦203726 have one of¦203727 your descendants\add* ruling over¦203735 Yisrael¦203735.’
\v 19 \add ≈However,\add* if¦203737 you \add collectively\add* turn¦203739 away¦203739, and abandon¦203741 my rules and instructions¦203742 that¦203744 I¦203745 gave you, and \add ≈decide to\add* serve¦203748 other¦203750 gods¦203749 and worship¦203751 them¦203752,
\v 20 then¦203754 I'll remove \add @these people¦203775\add* from¦203755 my¦203756 land¦203756 that I gave¦203758 them¦203759. \add ≈Also¦203754 this¦203763 temple\add* that I consecrated¦203765 for¦203766 \add ≈myself\add*, I'll \add ≈throw¦203767 it away where I can't see it\add*, and I'll make¦203770 it \add ≈an object of scorn and ridicule\add* among all¦203773 the¦203775 \add other\add* nations¦203775.
\p
\v 21 Then¦203777 this¦203778 \add ≈temple, which¦203779 everyone¦203784 admires\add* as they pass¦203784 by¦203784, will be¦203786 devastated, and \add @people\add* will \add ≈ask\add*, ‘Why did¦203789 Yahweh¦203790 do¦203789 \add ≈such terrible things\add* to that \add ≈temple\add* and to that land¦203792?’
\p
\v 22 ‘It happened because they abandoned¦203800 Yahweh¦203803, their¦203806 ancestors'¦203806 god¦203805,’ others will reply. ‘He¦203808 brought¦203808 them out¦203808 from¦203809 \add slavery in\add* Egypt¦203810, \add ≈but¦203797 then¦203797\add* they obtained other¦203813 gods¦203812 and worshipped¦203814 them and served¦203816 them—that's why he¦203820 sent them all¦203823 this¦203826 misery.’ ”
\c 8
\s1 King Shelomoh's achievements
\rem /s1 Solomon's Many Achievements; Solomon's Achievements; Solomon's Other Activities; Various Activities of Solomon
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 9:10-28)
\p
\v 1 \add ≈After\add* the twenty¦203832 years¦203833 that¦203834 it took Shelomoh¦203836 to build¦203835 Yahweh's¦203840 \add ≈temple\add* and¦203841 his¦203843 \add ≈palace\add*,
\v 2 \add *he\add* rebuilt¦203850 the cities¦203845 that¦203846 \add King\add* Huram¦203848 had¦203847 given¦203847 to \add *him\add*, and¦203845 he \add ≈got Israelis¦203857 to live in them\add*.
\p
\v 3 Then¦203860 Shelomoh¦203861 \add ≈attacked\add* Hamat¦203863-Tsovah and¦203860 \add ≈captured¦203864 it\add*.
\v 4 He¦203867 \add ≈rebuilt\add* Tadmor¦203870 in the wilderness¦203871, and¦203872 storage¦203876 cities¦203875 in the Hamat¦203879 \add region\add*.
\v 5 He¦203881 \add ≈rebuilt\add* the fortified¦203893 cities¦203892 of Upper-Beyt-Horon and Lower-Beyt-Horon with walls¦203894 and barred gates,
\v 6 as well as Baalat and all the storage¦203905 cities, and all the cities for Shelomoh's¦203908 chariots¦203913 and horsemen¦203916 that¦203906 he¦203924 wanted to¦203925 build¦203925 in¦203926 Yerushalem¦203926 and Lebanon¦203927, and throughout his kingdom.
\v 7 All the people¦203934 \add ≈who lived in Yisrael¦203945 but¦203939 who were actually\add* remnants of the Hittites¦203938, Amorites¦203939, Perizzites¦203940, Hivites¦203941, and Yevusites,
\v 8 \add ≈who were descendants¦203950 of groups that the Israelis¦203959 hadn't completely destroyed¦203958, were forced¦203963 to become Shelomoh's¦203962 labourers¦203963, and¦203961 they¦203952 still continue in that role\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈However¦203971,\add* Shelomoh¦203976 didn't¦203973 make¦203975 the¦203970 Israelis¦203970 become labourers, because¦203979 they¦203981 became his¦203978 \add ≈soldiers\add*, officers¦203985, chariot¦203987 commanders, and¦203968 horsemen¦203988.
\v 10 \add ≈Some\add* 250 \add Israelis\add* were¦203992 \add also\add* King¦203998 Shelomoh's¦203999 \add ≈chief officials¦203993\add* who had authority¦204002 over the people¦204003.
\p
\v 11 Shelomoh¦204011 brought¦204010 \add his wife\add*, Far-oh's¦204009 \add !(Pharaoh's¦204009)\add* daughter¦204007, up¦204010 from¦204012 the city¦204012 of David to the house¦204014 he'd built¦204016 for¦204018 her¦204018, because he said¦204020, “My wife mustn't live in¦204026 the \add ≈palace\add* of Yisrael's¦204030 King¦204028 David, because the places¦204035 where¦204035 Yahweh's¦204040 box¦204039 has¦204037 been are sacred¦204033.”
\p
\v 12 Then¦204050 Shelomoh¦204045 sacrificed burnt¦204046 offerings¦204044 to¦204047 Yahweh¦204047 on¦204048 the altar¦204049 that¦204051 had¦204052 been built¦204052 in¦204053 front¦204053 of¦204053 the \add temple's\add* porch¦204054.
\v 13 He \add ≈followed Mosheh's¦204062 instructions about¦204056 the daily\add* \add sacrifices\add* for the rest days and the new moons¦204064, and for the three¦204066 appointed occasions¦204067 each year¦204068: the Festival of¦204069 Flat Bread¦204070, the Harvest Festival, and the Celebration Living in¦204056 Shelters.\x + \xo 8:13: a \xt Num 28:9-10; \xo b \xt Num 28:11-15; \xo c \xt Exo 23:14-17; 34:22-23; Num 28:16–29:39; Deu 16:16.\x*
\v 14 Then¦204076, as his father¦204080 David had instructed, he assigned the priests to divisions for their various tasks, and the Levites¦204088 who would praise¦204092 and minister¦204093 in front¦204094 of the priests and help in their daily tasks, and gatekeepers¦204100 in their divisions at¦204101 the various gates. \add All\add* that was what David, the man¦204108 of God, had commanded¦204106.
\v 15 The priests¦204118 and¦204112 Levites¦204119 followed the king's¦204115 instructions concerning¦204123 all their duties, as well as \add their supervision of\add* the treasuries¦204123.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦204125 now,\add* all¦204126 of¦204126 Shelomoh's¦204129 work¦204128 on Yahweh's¦204136 \add ≈temple\add* was¦204125 completed—from the foundation¦204133 through to its¦204126 completion \add and operation\add*.
\p
\v 17 Then¦204145 Shelomoh¦204147 went¦204146 to Etsyon-Gever and¦204151 to Eylat on¦204154 the edge of¦204156 the ocean, in¦204158 the Edom¦204159 \add ≈region¦204158\add*.
\v 18 \add King\add* Huram¦204164 \add (from Tsor/Tyre)\add* sent¦204161 ships to him¦204163, \add as his\add* servants knew¦204171 the sea¦204172 \add well\add*. Then¦204161 Shelomoh's¦204177 men \add boarded the ships\add* and sailed with¦204165 them to Ofir¦204178, where they¦204179 obtained fifteen tonnes of¦204185 gold¦204186 and brought¦204187 \add it back\add* to King Shelomoh.
\c 9
\s1 The queen from Sheva visits
\rem /s1 The Queen of Sheba Visits Solomon; The Queen of Sheba's Visit; The Visit of the Queen of Sheba; Visit of the Queen of Sheba
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 10:1-13)
\p
\v 1 The¦204194 queen¦204194 from the¦204200 Sheva¦204196 \add region\add* had heard¦204197 \add ≈all about¦204194\add* Shelomoh, and she¦204202 came to Yerushalem¦204208 with some hard questions¦204207. Her¦204232 party \add included\add* a large number¦204216 of camels¦204212 carrying¦204213 lots of spices¦204214 and gold¦204215 and valuable gemstones. She¦204219 came to Shelomoh and \add ≈discussed\add* with him¦204224 everything that¦204213 was¦204229 on¦204207 her¦204232 mind¦204232.\x + \xo 9:1-9: \xt Mat 12:42; Luk 11:31.\x*
\v 2 Shelomoh¦204237 responded to all¦204240 her¦204242 \add ≈queries\add*, and¦204243 there wasn't any subject that¦204248 \add *he¦204249\add* wasn't able to speak about¦204240.
\v 3 When¦204253 the queen¦204254 from Sheva¦204256 saw Shelomoh's¦204259 wisdom¦204258, and¦204260 \add ≡saw\add* the \add ≈palace\add* that¦204261 he'd built¦204262
\v 4 and the food¦204264 at his table¦204265, as well as his servants'¦204269 stations¦204266, his well-dressed ministers standing¦204268 by, his cup-bearers¦204271 in¦204282 their¦204272 uniforms, and the burnt¦204273 offerings¦204273 that¦204274 he sacrificed at Yahweh's¦204277 \add ≈temple\add*, it¦204280 \add ≈took her¦204282 breath¦204283 away\add*
\v 5 and she¦204285 told the king¦204288, “Everything I¦204292 heard¦204292 in¦204293 my¦204293 \add own\add* country about¦204293 you and your¦204299 wisdom¦204299 was true.
\v 6 I didn't believe¦204303 \add ≈what they¦204309 reported to¦204304 me¦204315 until¦204305 I saw¦204309 it¦204313 with my¦204310 own¦204310 eyes¦204310\add*, and¦204301 wow, the reports¦204304 I heard¦204324 \add ≈didn't even cover\add* \em half\em* the extent of your¦204318 wisdom¦204318!
\v 7 Your men¦204327 are blessed, and \add even\add* your servants¦204329 are blessed to be able to continually¦204333 stand¦204331 in front¦204332 of you and listen¦204334 to your wisdom¦204337.
\v 8 Your god Yahweh¦204340 ought to be blessed¦204342—the one who¦204343 delighted¦204345 in¦204346 you and placed you on¦204346 his throne¦204350 as \add *his\add* king. Your god¦204341 loved¦204354 Yisrael¦204358 \add and wanted\add* to establish¦204359 them forever¦204360, \add ≈so\add* he's¦204361 placed you over¦204362 them as king—to give justice¦204365 and \add ≈do¦204364 what's right¦204366\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then¦204368 she¦204386 gave the king¦204369 four tonnes of gold¦204374, a very large quantity of spices, and¦204368 valuable gemstones. \add Nobody before had ever seen\add* such a large amount of spices as what the queen¦204387 from Sheva¦204389 gave to¦204390 King¦204369 Shelomoh¦204391.
\p
\v 10 (\add ≈Also¦204393\add*, \add King\add* Huram's¦204396 servants \add working together with\add* Shelomoh's¦204399 servants brought¦204402 gold¦204403 from¦204404 Ofir¦204404, as well as algum¦204407 wood and¦204393 valuable gemstones.
\v 11 The¦204412 king made¦204411 the algum¦204416 wood into staircases for Yahweh's¦204420 \add ≈temple\add* and for the king's¦204422 \add ≈palace¦204421\add*, and into lyres¦204423 and harps¦204424 for the singers¦204425. Nothing like that had¦204428 been seen¦204428 before¦204430 in¦204431 Yehudah¦204432.)
\p
\v 12 King¦204434 Shelomoh¦204435 gave¦204436 the queen¦204437 from¦204447 Sheva¦204439 \add ≈everything she wanted\add*—more than what she'd brought¦204450 to the king¦204453. Then¦204434 she \add ≈departed\add* with her servants¦204458 and¦204434 went¦204455 \add back\add* to her country.
\s1 Shelomoh's wealth
\rem /s1 Solomon's Great Wealth; Solomon's Wealth and Splendour; King Solomon's Wealth; Solomon's Splendour
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 10:14-25)
\p
\v 13 In¦204468 one¦204469 year¦204468, Shelomoh¦204467 received about¦204462 twenty tonnes of¦204474 gold¦204475,
\v 14 as well as what¦204478 the merchants¦204479 and traders¦204480 brought in. All the Arabian¦204485 kings¦204484 and all the \add ?≈local\add* governors¦204486 brought gold¦204489 and silver¦204490 to¦204491 Shelomoh¦204491.
\v 15 King¦204494 Shelomoh¦204495 made¦204493 two¦204496 hundred large shields of beaten gold—six¦204500 hundred gold \add coins' worth\add* of beaten gold \add ≈went into\add* each shield¦204507.
\v 16 \add ≈Also¦204528,\add* three hundred \add ≈smaller shields\add*—three hundred gold \add coins' worth\add* of beaten¦204515 gold \add ≈went into\add* each shield¦204522.
\p
\v 17 Then the¦204532 king¦204532 made¦204531 a large¦204536 ivory¦204535 throne¦204533 and¦204537 overlaid¦204537 it¦204537 with pure¦204539 gold¦204538.
\v 18 There were six¦204541 steps¦204542 \add leading up to\add* the throne¦204543, and¦204541 a gold¦204545 footstool¦204544 was attached¦204547 to \add *it\add*. It had an armrest on¦204545 \add ≈each side\add*, with¦204545 a lion \add statue\add* beside¦204558 each armrest.
\v 19 There were twelve \add statues of\add* lions¦204563 standing¦204564 on¦204566 the six¦204568 steps¦204569—one at each end of each step. \add No throne\add* like that¦204570 existed in any¦204576 other¦204571 kingdom¦204578.
\p
\v 20 All¦204580 of King¦204583 Shelomoh's \add ≈cups\add* were made of gold, and¦204580 all¦204586 the \add ≈various dishes\add* in ‘The House¦204588 of the Lebanon¦204591 Forest¦204590’ were refined gold. Nothing was¦204596 made of silver, because \add ≈during¦204597\add* Shelomoh's \add reign\add*, silver wasn't considered valuable,
\v 21 because¦204601 the king's¦204604 ships¦204615 went¦204613 to Tarshish¦204606 with Huram's¦204609 servants¦204608. Every¦204616 three¦204611 years¦204612 the fleet would \add ≈bring back\add* gold¦204618, silver¦204619, ivory, and apes and baboons,
\v 22 \add ≈so\add* King¦204626 Shelomoh¦204627 \add became\add* greater¦204625 than all¦204628 the other kings¦204629 in the world, \add both\add* in wealth¦204631 and¦204632 in wisdom¦204632.
\p
\v 23 \add ≈Kings¦204635 from all¦204634 over the world wanted to come and¦204634 listen¦204642\add* to the wisdom¦204645 that¦204646 God¦204649 had¦204648 \add ≈given\add* Shelomoh¦204641.
\v 24 Each¦204654 of them would bring¦204653 gifts: gold¦204659 and silver¦204657 items, clothes¦204660, myrrh and spices¦204662, horses¦204663 and mules¦204664. (\add This continued\add* \add ≈year after year\add*.)
\p
\v 25 Shelomoh¦204672 had four¦204673 thousand stalls¦204675 for horses¦204676 and chariots¦204677, and twelve thousand horsemen¦204682, and he¦204683 kept \add some\add* in the chariot¦204685 cities¦204684 and \add some\add* \add ≈close by\add* in Yerushalem¦204689.\x + \xo 9:25: \xt 1Ki 4:26.\x*
\v 26 He¦204691 \add ended up\add* ruling¦204692 over all the kings¦204695 \add in the region\add*, from¦204696 the \add Euphrates\add* River¦204698 \add in the northeast\add*, \add west\add* to the area of¦204701 the Philistines¦204702, and¦204691 \add south down\add* to the Egyptian¦204705 border¦204704.\x + \xo 9:26: \xt Gen 15:18; 1Ki 4:21.\x*
\v 27 The¦204712 king¦204708 made¦204716 silver¦204711 \add as common\add* as stones¦204713, and¦204714 cedar¦204715 \add timber as common\add* as the sycamore¦204717 fig trees in¦204712 the lowlands.
\v 28 Horses¦204724 were¦204723 brought¦204723 in from Egypt¦204725 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* for¦204726 Shelomoh¦204726, and¦204727 from \add ≈other countries¦204729 as well\add*.\x + \xo 9:28: \xt Deu 17:16.\x*
\s1 Summary of Shelomoh's reign
\rem /s1 Summary of Solomon's Reign; Death of Solomon; Solomon's Death
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 11:41-43)
\p
\v 29 Everything else that Shelomoh¦204733 did, from the beginning to the end, was written down by the prophet Natan¦204743, and in the prophecy¦204747 by Ahiyah¦204748 (from Shiloh), and the prophet Iddo's¦204751 visions¦204750 about¦204731 Nevat's¦204759 son¦204757 Yaraveam¦204756 \add !(Jeroboam¦204756)\add* \add were also written down\add*.
\v 30 Shelomoh¦204762 reigned¦204761 from Yerushalem¦204763 over¦204764 all¦204766 of¦204766 Yisrael¦204768 for forty¦204769 years¦204770,
\v 31 then¦204772 he¦204772 \add ≈died\add* and was buried¦204777 with¦204778 his father¦204780 in¦204778 ‘The¦204773 City¦204778 of David¦204779’, and his son¦204783 Rehaveam¦204782 \add !(Rehoboam¦204782)\add* \add ≈replaced him¦204777 as king¦204781\add*.
\c 10
\s1 Yisrael splits in two
\rem /s1 Kings of Judah; The Revolt against Rehoboam; Israel Rebels Against Rehoboam; The Northern Tribes Revolt
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 12:1-20)
\p
\v 1 Then¦204788 Rehaveam¦204788 \add !(Rehoboam¦204788)\add* went¦204787 to¦204789 Shekem¦204789, where all¦204793 of¦204793 Yisrael¦204795 had¦204792 gathered \add ≈for his coronation\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈Meanwhile\add*, Nevat's¦204804 son¦204802 Yaraveam¦204801 \add !(Jeroboam¦204801)\add* had¦204808 fled¦204808 from King¦204811 Shelomoh¦204810 and¦204799 was \add down\add* in¦204806 Egypt, \add ≈but¦204799\add* when he heard¦204800 \add about the coming coronation\add*, \add *he\add* returned¦204812 from Egypt.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦204816\add* the leaders of the northern tribes summoned¦204817 \add @Yaraveam¦204821\add*, and he¦204820 went¦204820 with them to speak¦204825 to \add Shelomoh's son\add* Rehaveam¦204828 and all¦204822 of Yisrael¦204824, saying¦204829,
\v 4 “Your father \add ≈made us work¦204838 very hard¦204832, but¦204836\add* now¦204836, lighten¦204837 the¦204838 \add ≈demands that¦204843\add* your father \add ≈made on¦204846\add* us, and¦204847 we'll¦204847 serve¦204847 you¦204847.”
\p
\v 5 “Come back to me¦204855 in three¦204852 days¦204853.” \add @Rehaveam\add* \add ≈answered¦204849\add*, so the¦204857 people¦204857 departed.
\p
\v 6 Then King¦204861 Rehaveam¦204862 consulted¦204860 with¦204873 the older men who'd advised his¦204872 father¦204872 Shelomoh¦204871 when¦204873 he was \add still\add* alive¦204874, \add ≈asking\add* \add &them\add*, “How¦204876 do you advise me to answer the people¦204880?”
\p
\v 7 “If¦204888 you're good¦204891 to those people¦204892 and \add ≈do things that¦204893 please¦204894 them\add*, and speak¦204895 \add ≈kindly\add* to them,” they \add ≈answered\add*, “then¦204885 they'll¦204899 \add ≈serve you for a long time¦204904 to come\add*.”
\p
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Rehaveam\add* \add ≈rejected¦204906 their advice\add*, and¦204906 consulted¦204913 some of¦204909 the young men \add ≈there\add* who'd grown¦204918 up¦204918 with¦204919 him.
\v 9 “\add ≈How would you¦204926 guys suggest I answer the people¦204932 who've asked me¦204936 to lighten¦204938 the burden on¦204946 them, compared to my father's¦204945 time\add*?”
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈Those¦204964 people¦204958 tell you that your father was hard on¦204971 them and¦204948 that you should lighten¦204970 their load\add*,” \add ≈his contemporaries advised him\add*. “\add ≈But¦204948 you should tell them that your little¦204975 finger¦204975 is¦204976 thicker¦204976 than¦204977 your father's¦204978 waist\add*,
\v 11 \add ≈and¦204980 that whereas he required them to¦204988 contribute, you'll be even more demanding. Tell them that he might\add* have whipped them with \add leather\add* whips¦204994, but¦204980 that you'll whip them with scorpions¦204996!”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So\add* Yaraveam¦205000 and all¦205001 the people¦205003 \add ≈returned¦205013\add* to¦205004 \add King\add* Rehaveam¦205006 on the third day \add ≈as he'd prearranged\add*,
\v 13 and¦205018 ignoring the advice of the older men, the king answered¦205018 \add @the people\add* harshly.
\v 14 \add ≈He¦205028 passed on¦205043 the younger men's suggestion\add*, telling \add &the people\add*, “I'll make¦205033 your \add ≈burden even heavier\add*. My¦205040 father¦205040 rebuked you \add people\add* with whips¦205043, but¦205028 I'll \add ≡do it\add* with scorpions¦205045.”
\v 15 \add ≈So¦205047\add* the king¦205050 \add ≈took no notice of the people's¦205053 request\add*, because¦205054 \add ≈it¦205056 was God turning¦205057 events around, so¦205060 that¦205066 what Yahweh¦205062 had¦205067 said to Yaraveam¦205073 (Nevat's¦205076 son¦205074) through Ahiyah¦205069 (from Shiloh) would come to pass\add*.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈When¦205078\add* all \add ≈the Israelis¦205088\add* saw that the king hadn't listened¦205084 to them¦205086, the people¦205088 \add from the northern tribes\add* answered¦205087 the king, “What¦205094 \add ≈did David have to do with¦205098 us anyway\add*? \add ≈We had¦205084 nothing to gain\add* from Yishay's¦205104 \add !(Jesse's¦205104)\add* son¦205102. \add ≈You might as well all head home, and¦205078 then¦205078 they'll see what happened to David's¦205098 dynasty\add*.”
\p \add ≈So¦205078 they all¦205078 went¦205112 home\add*,\x + \xo 10:16: \xt 2Sam 20:1.\x*
\v 17 and¦205119 Rehaveam¦205126 \add ended up\add* \add ≈only ruling over the Israelis¦205120 living¦205121 in¦205122 the Yehudah¦205123 region\add*.
\p
\v 18 King Rehaveam \add (still in Shekem)\add* sent¦205128 out Hadoram¦205133, his supervisor of the forced labourers¦205137, but¦205128 the \add ≈Israelis¦205141 hurled stones¦205138 at¦205150 him and killed him\add*. \add When he heard about that\add*, King Rehaveam¦205130 \add ≈forced his way into his\add* chariot¦205150 \add ≈and escaped\add* to Yerushalem¦205152,
\v 19 and¦205155 \add northern\add* Yisrael¦205156 has¦205155 rebelled¦205155 against David's¦205158 \add ≈descendants\add* to¦205159 this¦205161 day¦205160.
\c 11
\s1 The scolding of prophet Simayass to Rehoboam
\rem /s1 Judah and Benjamin Fortified; Shemaiah's Prophecy
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 12:21-24)
\p
\v 1 When¦205165 Rehaveam \add !(Rehoboam¦205165)\add* \add ≈arrived in\add* Yerushalem¦205166, he assembled¦205167 Yehudah's¦205171 and Benyamin's¦205172 \add ≈warriors\add*: 180,000 chosen¦205176 to fight¦205179 against Yisrael¦205182 to bring the¦205186 kingdom¦205186 back to Rehaveam.
\v 2 \add ≈But¦205199\add* Yahweh¦205193 \add ≈spoke\add* to¦205194 the prophet Shemayah¦205196, saying¦205200,
\v 3 “\add Go and\add* tell \add ≈this\add* to Shelomoh's¦205208 son¦205206 King¦205209 Rehaveam¦205205 of Yehudah, and to all¦205212 the Israeli¦205212 people from the Yehudah and Benyamin¦205216 tribes:
\v 4 Yahweh says¦205220 that you mustn't go and fight with¦205228 your relatives. Everyone¦205232 should just go home¦205233 again, because¦205234 everything¦205232 that's happened came from me¦205235.” \add ≈So\add* they listened to the message¦205242 from Yahweh, and \add ≈called off the planned attack\add* against¦205246 Yaraveam¦205248.
\s1 Rehaveam fortifies the cities
\rem /s1 Rehoboam Fortifies Judah; Rehoboam Fortifies the Cities
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So\add* Rehaveam¦205252 lived¦205251 in¦205253 Yerushalem¦205253 and fortified¦205256 the cities¦205255 throughout Yehudah¦205257:
\v 6 Beyt¦205262-Lehem, Eytam¦205267, Tekoa¦205270,
\v 7 Beyt¦205274-Tsur¦205276, Sokoh¦205279, Adullam¦205282,
\v 8 Gat¦205286, Mareshah¦205289, Zif¦205292,
\v 9 Adorayim¦205296, Lakish¦205299, Azekah¦205302,
\v 10 Zorah¦205306, Ayyalon¦205309, and Hevron¦205312 (all in¦205314 Yehudah¦205314 and Benyamin¦205315).
\v 11 He¦205319 strengthened¦205319 the¦205322 fortifications¦205322 \add in those cities and towns\add*, \add ≈appointed an army commander¦205325, and stocked their storehouses¦205326 with\add* food¦205327 and oil¦205328 and wine¦205329.
\v 12 He¦205337 \add also\add* \add ≈equipped each¦205331 of them¦205337 with\add* shields¦205335 and spears¦205336, and \add ≈made¦205337 sure they were well-protected\add*. \add ≈So¦205331\add* Yehudah¦205343 and Benyamin¦205344 \add ≈were under his control\add*.
\s1 Priests and Levites go down to Yehudah
\rem /s1 Priests and Levites Support Rehoboam; Priests and Levites Come to Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 13 The¦205347 priests¦205347 and¦205348 Levites¦205348 throughout all¦205350 of Yisrael¦205352 \add ≈supported Rehaveam from¦205355 every part of the country\add*.
\v 14 The¦205362 Levites¦205362 abandoned¦205361 their property¦205366 and their pastureland¦205365 and moved to Yerushalem¦205369 and across the rest of Yehudah¦205368, because¦205370 Yaraveam¦205373 and his¦205374 sons¦205374 \add ≈stopped¦205372\add* them from¦205375 serving¦205375 as¦205375 Yahweh's¦205376 priests¦205375.
\v 15 \add ≈Instead\add* \add @Yaraveam\add* established his own priests¦205381 for his hilltop shrines¦205382 and for the goat and calf \add idols\add* that¦205385 he'd made¦205386.\x + \xo 11:15: \xt 1Ki 12:31.\x*
\v 16 \add ≈As well as\add* \add @the priests and¦205388 Levites\add*, people from¦205389 all¦205389 the Israeli¦205390 tribes¦205390 \add ≈who¦205392 wanted to serve\add* Yisrael's¦205391 god¦205400 Yahweh came¦205402 to Yerushalem¦205403 to sacrifice¦205404 to Yahweh, their ancestors'¦205407 god.
\v 17 \add ≈So¦205409\add* they strengthened the kingdom¦205412 of¦205412 Yehudah¦205413, and as \add @the people\add* followed David's¦205426 and Shelomoh's¦205420 examples, they strengthened Rehaveam's¦205417 \add rule\add* for three¦205422 years¦205428.
\s1 Rehaveam's family
\rem /s1 Rehoboam's Family; Rehoboam's Marriages
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 18 Rehaveam¦205434 \add ≈married\add* Mahalat¦205438. She was the daughter of David's¦205445 son¦205443 Yerimot¦205442, and her mother was Avihayil¦205446, the daughter of Eliav¦205449 and \add ≈granddaughter\add* of Yishay¦205452 \add !(Jesse¦205452)\add*.
\v 19 \add ≈They had\add* \add three\add* sons¦205456: Yeush¦205459, Shemaryah¦205462, and¦205454 Zaham¦205465.
\v 20 After¦205467 her¦205467, he¦205468 \add ≈married\add* Avishalom's¦205474 daughter¦205472 Maakah¦205471, and they had \add four sons\add*: Aviyah¦205479, Attai¦205482, Ziza¦205485, and Shelomit¦205488.
\v 21 Rehaveam¦205491 loved¦205490 Maakah¦205494 \add ≈the¦205495 most out of his¦205501 eighteen¦205504 wives and sixty slave-wives\add*. He¦205510 fathered¦205510 twenty-eight¦205511 sons¦205513 and sixty daughters¦205515,
\v 22 \add ≈but¦205517\add* he¦205517 appointed¦205517 Maakah's¦205525 son¦205523 Aviyah¦205522 to¦205518 be the leader¦205526 of his¦205527 \add older and younger\add* brothers¦205527, because¦205528 \add ≈that would mark him¦205529 as the future\add* king¦205529.
\v 23 He wisely¦205531 sent his¦205535 \add other\add* sons¦205535 to fortified¦205543 cities¦205542 across all \add ≈the regions\add* in Yehudah¦205539 and Benyamin¦205540, \add ≈where he¦205544 set them up generously\add* and \add ≈asked the local people¦205549 to give¦205544 them wives¦205550\add*.
\c 12
\s1 Egypt attacks Yehudah
