\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 14:25-28)
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However¦205564,\add* after Rehaveam¦205555 \add !(Rehoboam¦205555)\add* \add ≈had become established¦205553 and in firm control of¦205556 his¦205556\add* kingdom¦205554, he¦205557 \add ≈and all¦205562 the people\add* abandoned¦205557 Yahweh's¦205561 instructions.
\v 2 Because¦205581 they¦205582 were unfaithful¦205582 to Yahweh¦205583, King¦205571 Shishak¦205574 from Egypt¦205577 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* came¦205573 \add to attack\add* Yerushalem¦205580 in¦205569 the fifth¦205570 year¦205569 of¦205575 Rehaveam's¦205572 \add reign\add*,
\v 3 with 1,200 chariots¦205587 and sixty¦205588 thousand¦205589 horsemen¦205590, along with a huge number¦205592 of troops, including¦205586 Egyptians, Libyans¦205599, Sukkites¦205600, and Kushites.
\v 4 He captured¦205603 Yehudah's¦205609 fortified¦205607 cities¦205606, then¦205603 moved towards Yerushalem¦205613.
\p
\v 5 Then the prophet¦205617 Shemayah and¦205622 the leaders¦205622 of Yehudah¦205623 who'd \add ≈fled\add* to Yerushalem¦205629 because of Shishak's¦205631 \add attacks\add* came¦205618 to Rehaveam¦205621. \add @Shemayah\add* told them¦205633, “Yahweh¦205637 says¦205636 that it was you \add people\add* who abandoned me¦205640, \add ≈so¦205634\add* now I've¦205644 also¦205641 abandoned you \add ≈to be defeated by\add* Shishak.”
\p
\v 6 Then¦205650 the king¦205654 and the Israeli¦205653 leaders¦205651 humbled¦205650 themselves¦205650 and said¦205655, “Yahweh¦205658 \add ≈always does what's right¦205656 and fair\add*.”
\p
\v 7 When¦205660 Yahweh¦205661 saw¦205660 that¦205662 they'd humbled themselves, \add ≈he gave this\add* message¦205665 to Shemayah¦205671, “They've humbled themselves, \add so\add* I won't destroy¦205676 them—my rage¦205684 won't pour¦205683 out on¦205660 Yerushalem¦205685 \add ≈through Shishak's¦205688 attack\add*, and¦205660 I'll¦205676 give¦205677 them \add ≈a way to recover\add* \add in the future\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈Nevertheless,\add* they'll become¦205691 his servants¦205694, and they'll \add ≈learn\add* \add the difference between\add* \add ≈serving me versus serving other nations' kings\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add ≈When\add* Egypt's¦205706 King¦205704 Shishak¦205703 \add ≈invaded\add* Yerushalem¦205709, he took the treasures¦205713 from Yahweh's¦205716 \add ≈temple\add* and¦205717 the king's¦205721 \add ≈palace\add*. He took everything¦205724 \add valuable\add*, \add ≈including¦205702\add* the gold¦205730 shields¦205729 that¦205731 Shelomoh¦205733 had¦205732 made¦205732.\x + \xo 12:9: \xt 1Ki 10:16-17; 2Ch 9:15-16.\x*
\v 10 King¦205736 Rehaveam¦205737 \add ≈replaced them with\add* bronze¦205740 shields¦205739, and¦205735 \add ≈distributed them to the leaders of the people who¦205747 guarded¦205746\add* the entrance¦205748 to the king's¦205750 \add ≈palace\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈After that, whenever the king went to Yahweh's¦205758 temple, the guards went with him carrying¦205761 those bronze shields. Then¦205752 when the king left again, they'd return¦205762 them to the guardroom¦205765\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Because\add* Rehaveam humbled¦205768 himself¦205768, Yahweh¦205773 \add ≈stopped being angry with¦205768 him\add* and¦205768 didn't¦205774 \add ≈eliminate\add* him, \add ≈so\add* things¦205780 were \add reasonably\add* good¦205781 in¦205768 Yehudah¦205778.
\rem /s1 Death of Rehoboam; Summary of Rehoboam's Reign
\p
\v 13 King¦205785 Rehaveam \add ≈consolidated his rule\add* in Yerushalem. He¦205788 reigned¦205788 \add ≈for a total¦205813 of\add* forty-one¦205792 years¦205794—seventeen¦205797 of which were from Yerushalem city¦205803, which Yahweh¦205807 had¦205806 chosen¦205806 from all the tribes¦205814 in Yisrael¦205815 \add as the place\add* to establish his \add ≈reputation¦205811\add*. (\add @Rehaveam's¦205786\add* mother¦205817 was¦205818 the Ammonitess, Naamah¦205818.)
\v 14 \add @Rehaveam\add* did evil¦205822 \add things\add* because¦205823 he¦205821 didn't¦205824 \add ≈make¦205821 it¦205821 his¦205826 priority to¦205827 get direction¦205825 from\add* Yahweh¦205830.
\p
\v 15 The \add ≈account of everything Rehaveam did while he was king, including¦205833 genealogical¦205846 records, was recorded in¦205841 the scrolls\add* written¦205840 by the prophets¦205843 Shemayah¦205842 and Iddo¦205844. Rehaveam and Yaraveam¦205849 \add ≈were¦205850 at¦205841 war with¦205841 each¦205850 other for his entire¦205850 reign\add*.
\v 16 Then¦205854 Rehaveam¦205855 \add ≈died\add*, he was buried¦205859 with¦205860 his ancestors¦205858 in¦205860 ‘The¦205860 City¦205860 of David¦205861’, and¦205854 his son¦205864 Aviyah¦205863 \add ≈replaced\add* him¦205865 as king¦205862.
\c 13
\s1 Aviyah defeats Yeroboam
\rem /s1 Abijah Reigns over Judah; Abijah King of Judah; Abijah's War with Jeroboam
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (1 Kgs 15:1-8)
\p
\v 1 In¦205868 the¦205871 eighteenth¦205869 year¦205868 of King¦205871 Yaraveam's¦205871 \add !(Jeroboam's¦205871) reign\add*, Aviyah¦205874 \add started his\add* reign over¦205875 Yehudah¦205877 \add !(Judah¦205877)\add*.
\v 2 He¦205881 ruled from Yerushalem¦205882 for three years¦205880. (His¦205884 mother¦205884 was¦205885 Uriel's¦205888 daughter¦205886 Mikayah¦205885 from Giveah.)
\p \add ≈However\add*, war¦205892 \add started\add* between¦205894 Aviyah¦205895 and¦205896 Yaraveam¦205897.
\p
\v 3 Aviyah¦205900 \add ≈launched the¦205903 attack\add* with four-hundred thousand \add ≈strong warriors\add*, and¦205899 Yaraveam¦205914 drew¦205915 up¦205915 in formation¦205915 against him¦205916 with eight-hundred¦205918 thousand \add ≈strong warriors\add* in his army.
\p
\v 4 Aviyah¦205928 \add ≈stood on¦205933 the top of\add* Mt¦205930. Tsemarayim¦205931 in¦205933 the Efrayim¦205934 hill-country and \add ≈shouted\add*, “Yaraveam¦205937 and all of Yisrael¦205940, listen¦205936 to me.
\v 5 \add ≈Don't you¦205943 all understand\add* that Yisrael's¦205949 god¦205948 Yahweh¦205946 \add ≈made a formal agreement¦205959\add* that the¦205948 kingdom of¦205948 Yisrael was given¦205950 forever¦205956 to David¦205952 and¦205958 his¦205958 descendants¦205958?
\v 6 \add ≈But¦205963\add* Nevat's¦205967 son Yaraveam¦205964, who was a servant¦205968 of David's¦205972 son Shelomoh¦205969, \add ≈took action\add* and¦205973 rebelled¦205973 against his¦205976 master¦205976,
\v 7 and \add ≈a bunch of¦205988 wicked good-for-nothings\add* gathered¦205978 around \add @Yaraveam\add* and \add ≈created a force\add* against¦205999 Shelomoh's¦205990 son¦205988, Rehaveam, when Rehaveam was¦205992 \add ≈still an inexperienced¦205994, young¦205993 man¦205993 and couldn't stand up to\add* them¦205999.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦206001\add* now¦206001 you \add Israelis\add* are saying¦206004 that you'll \add ≈stand against\add* the kingdom¦206007 \add ≈that Yahweh¦206008 established through\add* David's¦206011 descendants¦206010. \add ≈There are certainly many of you, and¦206001 you have\add* the gold¦206017 calves¦206016 that Yaraveam¦206021 made¦206019 as gods¦206022 for¦206020 you.
\v 9 Didn't you \add people\add* drive¦206025 out¦206025 the Levites¦206034, as well as Yahweh's¦206029 priests who were Aharon's¦206033 descendants¦206032? Then you \add ≈appointed¦206035\add* for¦206036 yourselves ‘priests’ like¦206038 they have in¦206045 \add other\add* countries, so that anyone¦206046 who comes¦206042 to¦206043 consecrate¦206043 himself by bringing a young bull¦206045 from the herd¦206048 and¦206049 seven¦206050 rams¦206049 can become a ‘priest¦206052’ of your non-gods.
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈But¦206057\add* as for us, Yahweh is our¦206059 god¦206059 and we haven't abandoned¦206061 him¦206061. Our priests¦206062 who¦206063 minister to¦206064 Yahweh are¦206062 Aharon's¦206066 descendants¦206065, and the¦206067 Levites¦206067 \add ≈assist them\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈Every morning and every evening\add*, they¦206070 sacrifice burnt¦206072 offerings¦206070 to Yahweh, and spiced incense¦206079. There's \add sacred\add* bread¦206083 on¦206073 the \add ≈display\add* table¦206086, and the lamps in¦206073 the gold¦206089 lampstand give light¦206091 every evening because¦206094 we're¦206097 following our¦206102 god¦206102 Yahweh's¦206071 instructions, \add ≈but¦206070\add* you \add people\add* have¦206104 abandoned¦206104 him¦206105.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦206107 listen!\add* God¦206125 is¦206108 \add ≈guiding us¦206108\add*, and¦206107 his¦206112 priests¦206112 will blast¦206114 their trumpets¦206113 to¦206115 signal¦206115 battle¦206115 against you \add people\add*. \add ≡Listen,\add* you Israelis¦206117: don't¦206119 fight against Yahweh¦206124, your ancestors'¦206127 god¦206125, because¦206128 you won't¦206119 succeed¦206131.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈But¦206133 meanwhile,\add* Yaraveam had¦206134 \add ≈sent\add* \add some men\add* around to¦206134 ambush them from behind, so they¦206140 were¦206140 \add both\add* in front¦206141 of¦206141 \add the army from\add* Yehudah¦206142 and¦206133 in ambush behind them.
\p
\v 14 When¦206146 \add the warriors from\add* Yehudah¦206147 turned¦206146, wow, \add ≈they realised they were being attacked from in¦206158 front¦206151 and¦206146 from\add* behind¦206152. They¦206148 \add ≈called\add* out¦206153 to¦206154 Yahweh¦206154 \add for help\add* \add ≈while\add* the priests¦206155 blew¦206156 their trumpets¦206156.
\v 15 Then¦206160 the men from Yehudah \add ≈shouted¦206160 a loud battle cry\add*, and God¦206167 defeated¦206168 Yaraveam¦206171 and all¦206172 of Yisrael¦206174 \add ≈in¦206164 front¦206175 of\add* Aviyah¦206176 and Yehudah.
\v 16 Yisrael's¦206182 \add ≈soldiers\add* fled¦206179 away from¦206183 Yehudah's¦206184 \add army\add*, and¦206179 God¦206186 \add ≈enabled Yehudah to defeat them¦206185\add*.
\v 17 Aviyah¦206191 and his¦206192 \add ≈men thrashed them badly\add*, and \add some\add* five-hundred thousand¦206201 of¦206197 their chosen¦206203 \add ≈warriors were killed¦206196\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈So¦206205\add* the Israelis¦206208 were subdued¦206205 at¦206209 that¦206210 time¦206209, and¦206205 the people¦206212 from Yehudah¦206213 were victorious¦206211 because¦206214 they¦206215 \add ≈trusted in¦206209\add* Yahweh¦206218, their¦206220 ancestors'¦206220 god¦206219.
\p
\v 19 Aviyah¦206223 chased after¦206224 Yaraveam¦206225 and they captured¦206226 from¦206227 \add @Yisrael\add* the cities¦206228 of Beyt¦206231-El, Yeshanah¦206239, and Efron¦206245, and their surrounding villages.
\v 20 Yaraveam¦206254 \add ≈never regained military strength¦206252\add* during Aviyah's¦206257 \add ≈reign\add*, and \add after a time\add* Yahweh¦206259 struck¦206258 him¦206258 \add with sickness\add* and he¦206260 died¦206260.
\p
\v 21 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Aviyah¦206264 \add ≈became more powerful\add*. He took¦206265 fourteen wives¦206268 for himself¦206263, and had twenty-two¦206272 sons¦206274 and sixteen daughters¦206277.
\v 22 The rest¦206280 of \add ≈what Aviyah¦206282 did, including¦206280 his sayings and¦206284 his behaviour, was written¦206285 down by\add* the prophet¦206287 Iddo¦206288.
\c 14
\s1 King Asa's rule over Yehudah
\rem /s1 King Asa Defeats the Ethiopians; Early Years of Asa's Reign; Asa Reigns
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 Then Aviyah \add ≈died\add*, and they buried him with his ancestors in ‘The¦206314 city of David’, and his son Asa¦206313 reigned in his place. \add ≈During his rule,\add* the \add ≈country was peaceful for\add* ten years.
\v 2 Asa did what was good and right in his god Yahweh's eyes—
\v 3 he¦206337 removed the \add ≈pagan\add* altars and the \add ≈hilltop shrines\add*, \add ≈smashed\add* the sacred \add stone\add* pillars, and cut the Asherah poles down.
\v 4 He¦206350 \add ≈ordered\add* \add the people in\add* Yehudah¦206354 to \add ≈worship\add* Yahweh, their ancestors' god, and to obey his instructions and regulations.
\v 5 He¦206383 removed all the hilltop shrines from Yehudah's¦206369 cities¦206367, and \add also\add* the incense altars, and the kingdom \add ≈was peaceful¦206372 under his rule\add*.
\v 6 He¦206387 fortified Yehudah's¦206388 cities¦206393, as the place was quiet without war during those¦206394 years, because¦206403 Yahweh¦206407 had given¦206410 him¦206409 \add ≈peace\add*,
\v 7 and he'd told Yehudah¦206424, “Let's build these¦206439 cities \add ≈with walls around them\add*, and towers, doors, and bars, \add while\add* the land's quiet \add ≈around\add* us, because we've \add ≈asked\add* our god Yahweh \add ≈for guidance\add*. We've \add ≈made our request\add*, and he's given us rest \add ≈on all our borders\add*.” \add ≈So\add* they built and they \add ≈prospered\add*.
\v 8 \add King\add* Asa had an¦206448 army¦206448 of three-hundred¦206452 thousand¦206449 men from Yehudah who carried large shields and spears, as well as 280,000 men from Benyamin who also carried shields, along with¦206448 bows and arrows. They were all \add ≈powerful warriors\add*.
\s1 The Ethiopian invasion repelled
\rem /s1 Ethiopian Invasion Repulsed
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 9 \add ≈But¦206460 then\add* Zerah the Kushite \add (or Ethiopian)\add* came out against them with¦206465 an army of a million \add soldiers\add* and three hundred chariots, and he \add ≈advanced\add* to¦206467 Mareshah¦206467.
\v 10 Asa¦206471 went out to \add ≈oppose\add* them, and they deployed for battle in¦206493 the Tsefatah valley near Mareshah.
\v 11 Then \add King\add* Asa¦206516 called out to his god Yahweh, “Yahweh, it \add ≈makes no difference to you if there's one against you, or one million\add*. Help us, Yahweh our god, because we rely on you, and we've come against this \add ≈massive force, trusting in your reputation\add*. Yahweh, you're our god—don't let \add ≈mere humans\add* prevail against you.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So\add* Yahweh¦206542 \add ≈helped Asa¦206524 and the army¦206544 from Yehudah to defeat\add* the Kushites, and \add *they¦206545\add* fled.
\v 13 Asa and his army chased them \add southwest\add* as far as Gerar¦206557. \add ≈So many\add* Kushites \add ≈were killed\add* that \add the rest\add* \add ≈couldn't save themselves\add*, because¦206558 they'd been \add ≈destroyed¦206551 in¦206576 front\add* of Yahweh¦206563 and his \add ≈army\add*, and the \add @men of Yehudah\add* carried away a large amount of plunder¦206565.
\v 14 They struck all the cities around Gerar, because \add ≈the Kushites there were terrified of Yahweh\add*. The \add @men from Yehudah\add* plundered all those cities, because they¦206583 \add ≈contained a lot of valuable goods\add*.
\v 15 They also attacked the \add Kushite\add* cattle \add ≈herdsmen\add*, as well as capturing lots of sheep and camels \add ≈before returning\add* to Yerushalem.
\c 15
\s1 Azaryah's prophecy gives courage to Asa
\rem /s1 Asa's Religious Reforms; Asa's Reforms; Asa's Reform
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 Then God's¦206598 spirit¦206598 came down onto Oded's¦206595 son¦206593 Azaryah¦206592,
\v 2 and he went¦206601 out¦206601 to \add King\add* Asa and told him, “Listen¦206606 to me¦206606, Asa, and all¦206608 of Yehudah¦206610 and Benyamin¦206611: Yahweh¦206612 is¦206613 with you \add southerners\add* when¦206614 you're¦206614 with him. And¦206616 if you look for him, you'll find¦206619 him, but¦206601 if you abandon him, he'll¦206619 \add also\add* abandon you.
\v 3 Yisrael¦206630 has been without the¦206633 true God \add ≈for a long time¦206628\add*, as there hasn't been a priest¦206636 teaching¦206637, so \add God's\add* instructions \add have been forgotten\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈However,\add* they turned¦206641 to Yisrael's¦206649 god¦206648 Yahweh¦206647 when they were in¦206642 distress¦206642, and \add ≈requested his help\add*, and he¦206651 \add ≈helped\add* them¦206652.
\p
\v 5 “In¦206654 those¦206655 times¦206654, it wasn't¦206656 \add ≈safe to travel away\add*, because¦206660 there¦206656 was¦206656 \add ≈wide unrest among\add* the inhabitants¦206666 of¦206666 the \add surrounding\add* \add ≈regions\add*.
\v 6 Nation crushed nation, and¦206669 city \add ≡crushed\add* city, because¦206675 God¦206677 \add sent them\add* \add ≈one trouble¦206678 after another\add*.
\v 7 But¦206683 you¦206683 \add southerners\add*, be strong¦206684 and¦206685 don't¦206685 give up \add ≈striving\add*, because¦206689 your¦206692 \add hard\add* work¦206692 will be rewarded¦206691.”
\p
\v 8 When \add King\add* Asa¦206696 heard¦206695 those¦206698 words¦206697 and the prophecy¦206699 from the prophet¦206701 Oded's¦206700 \add son\add*, he \add ≈took¦206703 courage\add* and removed¦206703 all the detestable¦206704 \add idols\add* from across Yehudah¦206708 and Benyamin¦206709, and from the cities¦206712 he'd captured¦206714 from the Efrayim¦206716 hill¦206715 country. \add ≈Also,\add* he repaired¦206717 the altar¦206720 to¦206723 Yahweh that¦206713 \add stood\add* in¦206723 front¦206723 of Yahweh's¦206721 temple.
\p
\v 9 He¦206727 assembled all¦206730 \add the people from\add* Yehudah and Benyamin¦206733, as well as the many people who'd joined them¦206735 from \add the tribes of\add* Efrayim¦206736, Menashsheh¦206737, and Shimeon¦206738. (Many people had¦206741 emigrated from Yisrael¦206743 \add into Yehudah\add* when¦206745 they¦206745 realised¦206745 that¦206746 his¦206749 god¦206749 Yahweh¦206748 was \add ≈helping\add* him¦206750.)
\v 10 They¦206753 gathered¦206753 \add together\add* in Yerushalem¦206754 in \add ≈June\add* of the¦206761 fifteenth year¦206757 of \add King\add* Asa's¦206762 reign¦206761
\v 11 and sacrificed¦206764 seven hundred¦206774 bulls to Yahweh¦206765 and seven thousand¦206777 sheep¦206775—\add all of which had come\add* from the \add recent\add* plunder¦206770.
\v 12 They¦206779 \add solemnly\add* \add ≈agreed to sincerely and¦206779 diligently devote themselves to\add* Yahweh¦206784, their ancestors'¦206786 god¦206785.
\v 13 \add They decided\add* that anyone who¦206795 didn't¦206796 \add ≈worship\add* Yisrael's¦206802 god¦206800 Yahweh¦206799 \add ≈must¦206798 be killed, man¦206810 or woman¦206813, regardless of whether or not they had an important position\add*.
\v 14 Together they¦206815 \add ≈loudly promised\add* that to¦206816 Yahweh¦206816, then¦206815 shouted¦206819 and blew trumpets¦206820 and horns¦206821,
\v 15 and all of Yehudah¦206826 \add ≈celebrated that promise because¦206830 they were totally sincere and committed. They asked Yahweh¦206842 to give¦206841 them guidance, which he did, and he enabled them to have peace throughout their country\add*.
\p
\v 16 King¦206852 Asa also¦206846 removed¦206853 his mother¦206849 Maakah¦206848 from \add her position as\add* queen¦206854 because she¦206857 made¦206857 a disgusting Asherah¦206858 \add pole\add*. Asa cut¦206860 down¦206860 \add ≈the pole\add* and crushed¦206865 it, and burnt¦206866 it at¦206867 the Kidron¦206868 brook,
\v 17 \add ≈although\add* they¦206873 didn't¦206871 remove¦206873 the¦206870 hilltop¦206870 shrines¦206870 from¦206874 Yisrael¦206874. \add ≈Nevertheless,\add* Asa¦206878 \add ≈maintained his singular devotion\add* \add to Yahweh\add* \add ≈for his whole¦206881 life\add*,
\v 18 and he¦206885 brought¦206885 his father's¦206889 sacred¦206888 things¦206888, and his own¦206890, into God's¦206892 \add ≈temple\add*—gold¦206894 and silver¦206893 items.
\v 19 There was¦206899 no more war¦206897 \add in Yehudah\add* until¦206900 the¦206905 thirty-fifth¦206903 year¦206901 of¦206906 Asa's¦206906 reign¦206905.
\c 16
\s1 Yisrael comes to invade Yehudah
\rem /s1 Troubles with Israel; Final Years of Asa's Reign; Alliance with Aram Condemned; Asa's Last Years
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (1 Kgs 15:17-22)
\p
\v 1 In¦206909 the thirty-sixth¦206910 year¦206909 of¦206913 \add King\add* Asa's¦206913 reign¦206912, Yisrael's¦206918 king Baasha¦206915 \add ≈invaded\add* Yehudah and built¦206922 Ramah¦206925 to \add ≈prevent anyone¦206928 from leaving or entering the land controlled by\add* Yehudah's¦206921 King Asa.
\v 2 Asa¦206935 took gold¦206937 and silver¦206936 from¦206938 the \add ≈temple\add* treasuries¦206938 and the king's¦206942 \add ≈palace\add*, and he¦206943 sent¦206943 \add it\add* to¦206944 King¦206940 Ben¦206946-Hadad¦206948 of¦206949 Aram¦206950 \add (modern Syria)\add*, who¦206951 lived¦206951 in¦206952 Damascus¦206952, \add ≈requesting\add*,
\v 3 “\add I want\add* a \add ≈peace treaty¦206969\add* between you and me, and between your \add ≈family\add* and \add ≈mine\add*. Listen, I've sent¦206963 gold¦206966 and silver¦206965 to you. Go \add and\add* break¦206968 your agreement¦206955 with¦206970 Yisrael's¦206974 King¦206973 Baasha¦206972, \add ≈so¦206975\add* he'll \add ≈give up¦206975 on¦206976 his attack\add* against¦206976 me.”
\p
\v 4 Ben¦206979-Hadad¦206981 \add ≈accepted\add* King¦206984 Asa's¦206985 \add ≈suggestion\add* and sent¦206986 his army captains \add to fight\add* against¦206994 Yisrael's¦206997 cities. They¦206998 struck Iyyon¦207001, Dan¦207004, and Hevel¦207006-Mayim¦207007, and all¦207009 the storehouses¦207011 in the Naftali¦207013 cities.
\v 5 \add ≈When¦207015\add* \add King\add* Baasha¦207017 heard¦207016 \add about that\add*, he stopped \add ≈fortifying\add* Ramah¦207022 and¦207015 \add ≈abandoned the¦207022 project\add*,
\v 6 \add ≈so\add* King¦207030 Asa¦207029 took¦207031 \add men there\add* from Yehudah¦207036. They carried¦207037 away all the \add building\add* stones¦207040 from Ramah¦207041, along with the timber¦207044 which¦207045 Baasha¦207047 had¦207046 been using, and used \add it all\add* to build Geva¦207052 and Mitspah¦207055 \add (north of Yerushalem)\add*.
\s1 Hanani's prophecy about coming wars
\rem /s1 The Prophet Hanani
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 7 At¦207058 that¦207059 time¦207058, the prophet Hanani¦207061 went¦207060 to¦207063 Yehudah's¦207067 King¦207066 Asa¦207065 and¦207068 told him¦207069, “Because¦207070 you relied¦207070 on the king of¦207073 Aram¦207074 \add ≈rather than\add* on your¦207080 god¦207080 Yahweh¦207079, the Aramean¦207088 king's¦207073 army¦207085 has¦207084 escaped¦207084 from¦207089 \add ≈being defeated by you\add*.
\v 8 Didn't the Kushites and the Libyans¦207093 \add ≈have a vast number¦207097 of\add* chariots¦207098 and horsemen¦207099? Yet because¦207102 you relied¦207102 on¦207102 Yahweh¦207105, he¦207106 \add ≈helped you defeat them¦207106\add*,
\v 9 because¦207126 Yahweh¦207110 \add ≈sees everything that's happening all¦207113 over the world, and he strengthens¦207116 the people who¦207119 trust him¦207111 completely¦207120\add*. You've been foolish¦207122 \add ≈in what you've¦207122 just done\add*, so from¦207127 now¦207127 on¦207123, you'll \add ≈be¦207128 facing\add* wars¦207130.”
\v 10 \add ≈But¦207132\add* \add King\add* Asa was¦207132 angry at¦207142 the¦207136 prophet, very angry, and had him¦207137 put¦207137 in¦207142 \add ≈prison¦207139\add*, and \add ≈after that¦207146\add* Asa oppressed¦207147 some¦207149 of¦207149 \add &his\add* people¦207151.
\s1 The end of Asa's reign
\rem /s1 The End of Asa's Reign; Asa's Disease and Death; Summary of Asa's Reign
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 15:23-24)
\p
\v 11 \add ≈All of Asa's¦207157 projects from the beginning of his reign to the end\add* are¦207161 written¦207161 in the scroll¦207164 about¦207156 the kings¦207165 of Yehudah¦207166 and¦207155 Yisrael¦207167.
\v 12 \add King\add* Asa¦207170 \add ≈got a disease¦207169 that started in\add* his feet¦207175 in the thirty-ninth¦207172 year¦207171 of¦207175 his reign¦207174. \add ≈Even as it got worse,\add* he¦207185 didn't¦207183 \add ≈try to get\add* Yahweh¦207188 \add to help him\add*, only doctors.
\v 13 Then¦207192 Asa¦207193 \add ≈died¦207197\add* in¦207198 the forty-first¦207199 year¦207198 of¦207201 his¦207201 reign¦207201,
\v 14 and he was buried¦207203 in the tomb¦207204 that \add ≈he'd had carved out\add* in ‘The¦207209 City¦207209 of David¦207210’. They¦207211 laid \add ≈his corpse on¦207204 a bed of prepared spices¦207215 and perfumes¦207218 that had been mixed¦207217 ready\add*. Then¦207203 they¦207220 lit \add ≈a large¦207224 bonfire\add* \add in his honour\add*.
\c 17
\s1 Yehoshafat becomes king
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat Rules in Judah; Jehoshaphat King of Judah; Jehoshaphat's Reign; Jehoshaphat Becomes King
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 Then \add @Asa's\add* son¦207232 Yehoshafat¦207231 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦207231)\add* \add ≈replaced him¦207233 as king¦207230\add*, and he strengthened¦207234 \add ≈their defenses\add* against Yisrael¦207237.
\v 2 He¦207239 placed¦207239 \add ≈troops\add* in all¦207242 of¦207244 Yehudah's¦207245 fortified¦207246 cities, and posted garrisons¦207248 across Yehudah and in the¦207251 cities in Efrayim¦207252 that¦207253 his¦207256 father¦207256 Asa¦207255 had¦207254 captured¦207254.
\v 3 Yahweh¦207259 \add ≈helped\add* Yehoshafat¦207262 because¦207263 he followed his ancestor David's¦207266 example¦207265 at¦207265 the beginning, and¦207258 didn't¦207269 \add ≈ask the Baals¦207271 for guidance\add*,
\v 4 because¦207273 he \add ≈asked\add* his father's¦207275 god¦207274, and he \add ≈followed God's¦207274 instructions rather than doing the¦207280 evil things that were done in¦207277\add* Yisrael¦207281.
\v 5 \add ≈So¦207283\add* Yahweh¦207284 \add ≈enabled him to maintain control of his¦207288\add* kingdom¦207287, and all¦207290 of Yehudah¦207292 brought¦207289 tribute¦207293 to Yehoshafat¦207294, \add ≈causing him to become very wealthy¦207298 and highly respected\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈He was completely devoted to doing what pleased\add* Yahweh¦207306, even removing¦207308 the \add ≈hilltop¦207303 shrines¦207311\add* and¦207303 the Asherah¦207314 \add poles\add* from¦207315 Yehudah¦207315.
\p
\v 7 In¦207318 the third year¦207318 of his reign¦207320 he¦207321 sent¦207321 his \add ≈officials¦207322\add*, Ben¦207323-Hayil, Ovadyah¦207326, Zekaryah¦207327, Netanel¦207328, and Mikayah¦207329, to teach¦207330 in¦207331 Yehudah's¦207332 cities¦207331.
\v 8 They were¦207334 accompanied by the Levites¦207335 Shemayah¦207336, Netanyah¦207337, Zevadyah¦207338, Asahel¦207339, Shemiramot¦207340, Yehonatan, Adoniyah, Toviyah¦207344, and Tov-Adoniyah, along with¦207348 two priests¦207351, Elishama and Yehoram¦207350.
\v 9 They¦207363 \add took\add* a scroll \add ≈with¦207354 Yahweh's¦207358 instructions written on¦207354 it\add*, and¦207353 went¦207359 around¦207359 Yehudah's¦207354 cities¦207362 teaching the people¦207365.
\s1 Yehoshafat's rise
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat's Greatness
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 10 All¦207378 the \add ≈surrounding\add* kingdoms¦207374 \add ≈were afraid\add* of Yahweh¦207370, \add ≈so\add* they¦207380 didn't¦207379 \add ≈attack\add* Yehoshafat¦207383.
\v 11 \add ≈Some\add* of the Philistines¦207387 brought tribute¦207390 to¦207389 Yehoshafat¦207389, \add ≈including¦207391 lots of\add* silver¦207391. Also¦207385, the Arabians¦207394 brought him¦207396 flocks¦207397 \add totalling\add* 7,700 rams¦207398 and¦207385 7,700 goats¦207403.
\v 12 \add ≈So\add* Yehoshafat¦207411 \add ≈continued to become¦207413 more powerful¦207413\add*, and¦207417 he¦207413 built¦207417 palaces in Yehudah¦207418, as well as storehouses¦207421 in the cities¦207420.
\v 13 He \add ≈accumulated many supplies¦207423\add* in¦207427 Yehudah's¦207428 cities¦207427.
\p He \add also\add* had \add ≈many powerful warriors¦207429\add* in Yerushalem¦207433.
\v 14 \add ≈These¦207435 are the¦207443 leaders and¦207444 numbers from each tribe\add*:
\li1 From the tribe of Yehudah¦207439, Adnah¦207442 was¦207443 the commander¦207440, and he had three-hundred¦207447 thousand¦207441 warriors,
\li1
\v 15 \add ≈His¦207454 assistant\add* Yehohanan¦207455 commanded¦207456 280,000,
\li1
\v 16 \add ≈Next was\add* Zikri's¦207469 son¦207467 Amasyah¦207466, who¦207470 volunteered¦207470 for¦207471 Yahweh¦207471 and¦207472 commanded two-hundred thousand¦207474 \add ≈warriors\add*.
\li1
\v 17 From¦207479 \add the tribe of\add* Benyamin¦207481, Elyada¦207484 led two-hundred thousand¦207491 \add men\add* equipped¦207486 with¦207485 bows¦207488 and¦207489 shields¦207489,
\li1
\v 18 \add ≈next to him¦207498 was\add* Yehozavad¦207497 with¦207498 180,000 equipped¦207503 for war¦207504.
\m
\v 19 Those were¦207508 the \add ones who\add* served¦207508 the king, \add ≈along with¦207517\add* the \add ones\add* the king had placed in¦207517 Yehudah's¦207521 fortified¦207518 cities¦207517.
\c 18
\s1 prophet Mikiyas and King Ahab
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat and Ahab; Micaiah Prophesies Against Ahab; Micaiah Predicts Failure; The Prophet Micaiah Warns Ahab
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (1 Kgs 22:1-28)
\p
\v 1 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦207525 \add ≈became¦207529 very wealthy¦207526, and¦207524 was¦207524 highly honoured¦207527\add*, \add ≈but¦207524 then\add* he¦207529 allied¦207529 himself by marriage to \add Yisrael's King\add* Ahav¦207530.
\v 2 \add ≈Some years¦207534 later,\add* he went¦207550 \add ≈up\add* to Ahav in Shomron¦207538 \add !(Samaria¦207538)\add*, and Ahav¦207537 sacrificed lots of¦207533 sheep¦207543 and cattle¦207544 for him and for the people¦207546 who were with¦207548 him, and he incited¦207549 him to \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207553-Gilead¦207554—
\v 3 Yisrael's¦207560 King Ahav¦207557 \add ≈suggested to\add* Yehudah's¦207565 King Yehoshafat¦207563, “Will¦207566 you¦207566 \add ≈join\add* me¦207567 to \add attack\add* Ramot¦207568-Gilead¦207569?”
\p “\add ≈Wherever you'll be, I'll be there\add*,” he \add ≈responded¦207556\add*. “Your¦207574 people \add ≈are like my own\add* people, and¦207556 \add we're\add* with¦207577 you in¦207577 battle¦207577.”
\v 4 \add ≈Then¦207579 he¦207579 added\add*, “\add ≈But¦207579 we should get Yahweh's¦207592 advice first\add*.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦207594\add* Yisrael's¦207597 king¦207595 gathered¦207594 four¦207601 hundred¦207602 \add of his\add* prophets¦207600 and¦207604 \add ≈asked\add* them¦207605, “Should we¦207606 \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207609-Gilead¦207610 or¦207612 not?”
\p “Go¦207616 \add ≈ahead\add*,” they¦207615 answered¦207604, “and God will¦207617 give¦207617 \add ≈victory to¦207605\add* the king.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦207622\add* Yehoshafat¦207623 \add ≈asked\add*, “Is¦207624 there¦207624 no prophet¦207626 of Yahweh¦207627 here¦207625 that¦207629 we¦207629 can \add ≈ask\add*?”
\p
\v 7 Yisrael's¦207635 king¦207633 told Yehoshafat¦207668, “\add There's\add* still¦207640 one¦207643 man¦207641 \add ≈who would ask\add* Yahweh¦207647, \add ≈but¦207632\add* personally I¦207649 hate¦207650 him because¦207651 \add ≈he never¦207653 prophesies¦207654 anything good¦207656\add* about¦207655 me—\add ≈it's always something\add* evil¦207661. He's Yimlah's son¦207664, Mikayah¦207663.”
\p “\add ≈You shouldn't¦207669 talk like that\add*,” said¦207667 Yehoshafat.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦207675\add* Yisrael's¦207677 king¦207676 \add ≈ordered\add* an official, “\add Get\add* Yimlah's son¦207686 Mikayah¦207684 \add here\add* \add ≈as quick¦207683 as possible\add*.”
\rem /s1 Micaiah Prophesies against Ahab
\p
\v 9 \add ≈Now\add* the kings of Yisrael¦207691 and Yehudah¦207695 were \add both\add* clothed¦207701 in their \add royal\add* robes and sitting¦207696 there on their thrones¦207700 near Shomron's¦207707 \add !(Samaria's¦207707)\add* entrance¦207705 gate¦207706. They were \add up\add* on a threshing¦207704 floor¦207704, and all¦207708 the prophets¦207710 were prophesying¦207711 \add ≈in front¦207712 of\add* them¦207712.
\v 10 Kenaanah's¦207719 son¦207717 Tsidkiyah¦207716 made¦207714 himself some iron¦207721 horns¦207720 and¦207723 said¦207723, “Yahweh¦207727 says¦207726 you'll¦207729 use these¦207728 to¦207715 gore¦207729 Aram¦207732 and destroy¦207735 them¦207735.”
\v 11 All¦207737 the rest of Ahav's prophets¦207739 agreed, saying¦207742, “\add Yes,\add* go¦207743 and attack Ramot¦207744-Gilead¦207745 and you'll succeed¦207746—Yahweh¦207748 will give¦207747 the king¦207750 \add ≈victory\add*.”
\p
\v 12 The¦207752 messenger¦207752 who¦207753 went¦207755 to fetch Mikayah¦207758 \add ≈warned\add* him¦207760, “Listen, the king¦207771 \add ≈is pleased¦207774 with what the other prophets¦207764 agreed on. Just say¦207761 the same as them¦207777 and¦207752 give a favourable message¦207775\add*.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈But¦207781\add* Mikayah¦207782 \add ≈responded¦207781\add*, “As sure as Yahweh¦207785 lives, I'll¦207794 only say what my¦207792 god¦207792 tells¦207791 me to say.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈When¦207796 he¦207796 got\add* to¦207797 the king, King¦207799 \add Ahav\add* \add ≈asked\add* him¦207802, “Mikayah¦207803, should we¦207804 \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207807-Gilead¦207808 for¦207809 battle¦207809, or¦207810 should I¦207812 \add ≈hold back\add*?”
\p “Go¦207804 \add ≈ahead\add* and¦207796 succeed¦207815,” he \add ≈answered¦207800\add*. “\add ≈You'll be¦207816 given¦207816 victory over them\add*.”
\p
\v 15 \add ≈But¦207819\add* the king¦207821 said¦207819 to him¦207820, “How¦207824 many¦207824 times¦207825 must¦207826 I keep making¦207827 you promise that you'll¦207831 \add ≈only¦207833 say what Yahweh¦207837 says—not just what I want to hear\add*?”
\v 16 \add ≈So¦207839\add* \add @Mikayah\add* \add ≈responded¦207839\add*, “I¦207840 saw¦207840 all of¦207843 Yisrael¦207845 scattered¦207846 on¦207866 the¦207849 hills¦207849 like¦207850 sheep¦207850 without shepherds¦207855, and¦207839 Yahweh¦207857 said¦207856, ‘\add ≈They don't¦207852 have any master¦207860, so they'll all just go home¦207865\add* in¦207866 peace¦207866.’ ”\x + \xo 18:16: \xt Num 27:17; Eze 34:5; Mat 9:36; Mrk 6:34.\x*
\p
\v 17 \add ≈Ahav remarked\add* to Yehoshafat¦207874, “Didn't I¦207876 tell you¦207877 that he¦207880 wouldn't prophesy¦207880 anything good¦207882 about¦207881 me—only \add ≈disaster¦207886\add*?”
\p
\v 18 \add ≈But¦207889\add* \add @Mikayah\add* \add ≈continued¦207889\add*, “\add ≈Well, listen¦207891 to what Yahweh says¦207889\add*. I¦207895 saw¦207895 Yahweh sitting¦207899 on his¦207902 throne¦207902, and¦207903 all¦207903 the¦207905 \add ≈heavenly¦207906 soldiers¦207905\add* standing¦207907 on \add ≈each¦207903 side of him\add*,
\v 19 and Yahweh¦207914 said¦207929, ‘Who'll entice Yisrael's¦207922 King¦207920 Ahav¦207919 so¦207924 he'll¦207923 \add ≈attack\add* and then¦207913 die¦207924 at¦207925 Ramot¦207925-Gilead?’ \add ≈Some suggested one thing, and others suggested something else\add*.
\v 20 Then¦207935 \add ?≈a\add* spirit¦207936 went¦207935 out¦207935 and stood¦207937 \add ≈in¦207946 front¦207938 of\add* Yahweh and said¦207940, ‘I¦207941 myself will¦207942 entice¦207942 him.’ ‘\add ≈How would you do it¦207943\add*?’ Yahweh \add ≈asked\add* him.
\v 21 \add @The spirit¦207951\add* \add ≈replied¦207948\add*, ‘I'll¦207949 go¦207949 and \add ≈inspire all¦207954 of Ahav's prophets¦207956 to tell lies\add*.’ Yahweh said¦207957, ‘\add ≈That'll work\add*. Go and do¦207963 it.’
\p
\v 22 “\add ≈So¦207967\add* now¦207967, listen. Yahweh placed a deceiving spirit¦207971 in¦207973 the¦207973 mouths¦207973 of those¦207975 prophets¦207974 of yours, and¦207976 Yahweh \add ≈has¦207977 decreed that you'll face\add* disaster.”
\p
\v 23 Then Kenaanah's¦207986 son¦207984 Tsidkiyah¦207983 \add ≈went¦207982 up to\add* Mikayah¦207990 \add ≈and slapped him hard\add* on the cheek¦207993, saying¦207994, “\add Yeah?\add* \add ≈Since when did Yahweh's¦208001 spirit¦207999 leave me and start speaking¦208003 to\add* you¦208004?”
\p
\v 24 “Well¦208008, you'll¦208013 find out \add soon\add*,” answered¦208006 Mikayah¦208007, “on¦208015 the day¦208010 when¦208012 you go¦208013 room by room \add in some house\add* to \add ≈try to hide¦208016\add*.”
\p
\v 25 “\add ≈Arrest\add* Mikayah¦208024,” \add ≈ordered King¦208019 Ahav\add*, “and return¦208025 him¦208025 to Amon¦208028 the¦208029 city¦208031 \add ≈governor\add*, and to \add ≈my\add* son¦208035 Yoash¦208034.
\v 26 \add ≈Tell them that the¦208042 king's¦208042 ordered that this¦208044 man be put¦208043 in¦208054 prison¦208046, and be given only strictly-rationed bread¦208048 and water¦208050 until¦208052 I¦208053 return¦208053 safely\add*.”
\p
\v 27 “If¦208058 you¦208061 return \add ≈safely\add*,” Mikayah¦208057 \add ≈retorted\add*, “then¦208056 Yahweh¦208066 mustn't have¦208065 spoken¦208065 to me¦208067.”
\s1 The death of Ahab
\rem /s1 Ahab Killed at Ramoth Gilead; The Death of Ahab; Defeat and Death of Ahab
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (1 Kgs 22:29-35)
\p
\v 28 \add ≈So\add* Yisrael's¦208077 King¦208075 \add Ahav\add* and Yehudah's¦208081 king Yehoshafat¦208078 went to Ramot¦208084-Gilead¦208085.
\v 29 \add ≈Ahav\add* told Yehoshafat¦208092, “\add ≈I'll¦208093 get changed\add*, \add so I'm not recognised\add*, and go¦208094 into the battle, \add ≈but¦208087 you wear¦208097 your¦208098 royal robe\add*.” \add ≈So¦208087\add* Yisrael's¦208089 king¦208100 disguised¦208093 himself¦208099, and they¦208102 went¦208102 into the battle.
\p
\v 30 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Aram's¦208106 king had¦208107 ordered¦208107 his chariot¦208111 commanders¦208107, “Only attack Yisrael's¦208130 king—\add ≈don't¦208116 bother fighting anyone else\add*.”
\v 31 \add ≈However,\add* when \add &those\add* chariot¦208136 commanders¦208135 saw¦208134 \add King\add* Yehoshafat, they¦208145 \add ≈mistook him for\add* Yisrael's¦208143 king¦208142, and \add ≈wheeled\add* around to fight¦208147 him, \add ≈but¦208133\add* Yehoshafat cried¦208148 out¦208148 \add to Yahweh for help\add*, and \add *he¦208151\add* helped¦208151 him—God¦208153 drew them¦208152 away¦208154 from¦208154 him,
\v 32 \add ≈because¦208160\add* when the chariot¦208159 commanders¦208158 \add ≈realised¦208157\add* that¦208160 it¦208163 wasn't Yisrael's¦208165 king¦208164, they¦208166 turned¦208166 back¦208166 from¦208167 \add chasing\add* him¦208167.
\v 33 \add ≈However,\add* one \add Aramean\add* \add ≈warrior drew¦208170 his bow¦208171 without knowing where Ahav was\add*, and struck¦208173 Yisrael's¦208177 king¦208176 \add ≈at¦208171 a joint in¦208171 his\add* armour¦208181. \add @Ahav\add* \add ≈ordered\add* the charioteer¦208183, “Turn¦208184 \add ≈around¦208184 and get me¦208187 out¦208187 of¦208185 here\add*, because¦208191 I've¦208192 been¦208192 seriously wounded¦208192.”
\v 34 The battle¦208195 \add ≈continued\add* for the whole day¦208196, and¦208194 Yisrael's¦208199 king¦208198 was propped up in¦208202 his chariot¦208202 \add ≈to¦208203 watch\add* the Arameans¦208204, \add ≈but¦208194 he¦208208 died¦208208 as the sun¦208211 was setting\add*.
\c 19
\s1 Yehoshafat gets scolded
\rem /s1 A Prophet Reprimands Jehoshaphat; Jehoshaphat Appoints Judges
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 Yehudah's¦208217 king¦208215 Yehoshafat¦208214 returned¦208213 safely to¦208218 his¦208220 home in¦208221 Yerushalem¦208222,
\v 2 \add ≈but¦208224\add* Hanani's¦208231 son¦208229, the prophet Yehu¦208228, \add ≈confronted\add* him, “Should you have helped¦208239 the wicked¦208238, and¦208224 befriended those¦208240 that¦208243 Yahweh hates¦208240? Yahweh's¦208241 angry with¦208243 you because of what you've done.
\v 3 \add ≈However, you have some good¦208251 points\add*, because¦208254 you removed¦208256 the Asherah¦208257 \add poles\add* from¦208258 the \add ≈country\add*, and¦208261 \add ≈you've¦208256 been sincere in wanting to¦208263 follow\add* God.”
\s1 The neneyimu of Hihusapat
\rem /s1 The Reforms of Jehoshaphat; Jehoshaphat's Reforms; Jehoshaphat Appoints Judges
\p
\v 4 Yehoshafat¦208267 lived¦208266 in Yerushalem¦208268, \add ≈but¦208266\add* one time he went¦208271 out¦208271 to the people¦208272 of¦208277 Beer¦208273-Sheva in the Efrayim¦208278 hill¦208277 country¦208277 and¦208266 \add ≈encouraged\add* them¦208279 back to Yahweh¦208282, their¦208284 ancestors'¦208284 god¦208283.
\v 5 He¦208286 appointed¦208286 judges¦208287 in¦208289 Yehudah's¦208292 fortified¦208293 cities¦208291 \add ≈to serve across the country\add*,
\v 6 and¦208312 he¦208297 told them, “\add ≈Take¦208308 care in¦208313 what¦208302 you do¦208305, because¦208306 as judges¦208300, you're not¦208307 serving people, but¦208297 serving Yahweh¦208311 when you make judicial decisions\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈So¦208316 revere Yahweh and¦208316 judge cases carefully, because¦208324 our¦208330 god¦208330 Yahweh doesn't tolerate injustice¦208331, partiality¦208332, or bribery¦208336\add*.”
\p
\v 8 Yehoshafat¦208341 also¦208338 appointed¦208340 some Levites¦208344 and¦208338 priests¦208345 in Yerushalem, as well as \add ≈leaders\add* from some Israeli¦208348 families¦208347, to be judges¦208349 \add ≈on¦208339 Yahweh's¦208350 behalf based in\add* Yerushalem,
\v 9 and he¦208355 \add ≈instructed¦208355\add* them¦208356, “You \add ≈must¦208359 revere Yahweh¦208361 and be trustworthy and sincere\add*.
\v 10 When¦208366 any of¦208373 your \add ≈fellow Israelis\add* who¦208375 live¦208375 in¦208376 the cities¦208376 bring any case¦208368 to you \add ≈involving violent crime, or interpreting laws or regulations¦208386, and so on, you must¦208371 caution them so they¦208391 won't sin against Yahweh¦208392 and induce his anger¦208395 to come¦208371 against you or them, so do¦208401 that¦208369, and you won't be¦208403 guilty¦208403\add*.
\v 11 And listen, the chief¦208408 priest¦208407 Amaryah¦208406 is superior to you \add judges\add* in any \add ≈religious\add* matter, and Yishmael's¦208417 son¦208415 Zevady is \add ≈Yehudah's¦208421\add* leader¦208418 for any \add ≈civil\add* matter \add ≈concerning\add* the king¦208425. \add ≈Also¦208405\add*, you have the Levite¦208427 officials¦208426 to assist you \add judges\add*. \add ≈Act¦208430 with courage, and let¦208431 Yahweh¦208413 assist people who are doing what's right\add*.”
\c 20
\s1 Yehoshafat handles a massive invasion
\rem /s1 War against Edom; Invasion from the East; War with Moab, Ammon, and Edom; Jehoshaphat Defeats Moab and Ammon
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Sometime after¦208439 that,\add* the Moavites and Ammonites, along with¦208448 some¦208450 of¦208450 the Meunites¦208450,\f + \fr 20:1 \ft Following the Septuagint for this.\f* came¦208442 to battle¦208454 against \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208453.
\v 2 \add Some men\add* came¦208456 and told¦208457 Yehoshafat¦208458, “A \add ≈huge¦208463 army\add* is¦208460 coming¦208460 from¦208464 Aram¦208466 beyond¦208464 the¦208464 \add Dead\add* Sea¦208465 to attack you¦208461, and take note: they're¦208467 \add already\add* in¦208468 Hatstson-Tamar, also known as Eyn¦208471-Gedi¦208472.”
\v 3 Yehoshafat¦208476 \add ≈was¦208474 alarmed and decided to request¦208480 advice from\add* Yahweh¦208481, and he¦208474 \add ≈ordered that all¦208487 of¦208487 Yehudah¦208489 should fast¦208484\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈So¦208491\add* Yehudah assembled¦208491 to \add ≈request¦208493 Yahweh's¦208494 help\add*—they¦208500 came¦208500 to Yerushalem from all¦208496 of¦208498 Yehudah's¦208492 cities¦208498 to \add ≈ask Yahweh for help\add*.
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat's Prayer and Victory
\p
\v 5 Yehoshafat¦208507 stood¦208506 in front of all the people from Yerushalem¦208510 and¦208510 across Yehudah¦208509, in front of the new¦208515 temple courtyard¦208514,
\v 6 and \add ≈prayed\add*, “Yahweh¦208518, the god of our ancestors¦208520, aren't¦208521 you the god \add who lives\add* in the heavens¦208526? And¦208527 you rule in all¦208529 the kingdoms¦208530 \add ≈around the world\add*, and \add ≈you have full power¦208533 and control\add*—no one can stand¦208537 against¦208536 you.
\v 7 Weren't you our¦208542 god¦208542 who drove the previous inhabitants¦208546 of this¦208548 land¦208547 out ahead of your¦208550 Israeli people¦208550? Didn't you give¦208552 it¦208552 to¦208553 the descendants¦208553 of Abraham¦208554—the one you loved forever¦208556?\x + \xo 20:7: \xt Isa 41:8; Jam 2:23.\x*
\v 8 \add @Our ancestors\add* lived¦208558 in¦208560 \add @this land\add* and¦208561 built¦208561 a \add ≈temple to honour you\add*, saying¦208567,
\v 9 ‘If disaster, \add like\add* \add ≈war\add*, judgement¦208575, epidemic, or famine¦208577 comes¦208571 on¦208586 us, we'll stand¦208578 \add ≈in front of\add* this¦208582 \add ≈temple\add*, and \add ≈in front of\add* you, because¦208584 your¦208583 name¦208585 is¦208586 \add ≈honoured here\add*. And¦208588 we'll cry¦208588 to¦208589 you because of our¦208590 distress¦208590, and you'll¦208591 hear¦208591 and rescue us.’
\p
\v 10 You¦208606 didn't allow our Israeli¦208607 ancestors to enter the countries of Ammon¦208598, Moav¦208599, or Edom when¦208610 they were travelling from Egypt¦208612 \add to Canaan\add*. So¦208594 our ancestors turned¦208614 away from those areas and¦208594 didn't destroy¦208617 them, but¦208594 now¦208594 \add they're coming here to attack us\add*.\x + \xo 20:10: \xt Deu 2:4-19.\x*
\v 11 Look how they're¦208621 repaying¦208622 us \add for not destroying them\add*—they come¦208624 \add here\add* to¦208625 drive¦208625 us out¦208625 from¦208626 the \add ≈land\add* you¦208628 gave¦208628 us as an inheritance¦208628.
\v 12 \add So,\add* our¦208653 god¦208630, \add ≈please punish\add* them¦208634, because¦208635 \add ≈we're not¦208636 strong enough to battle this¦208642 huge¦208641 army that's on¦208634 its way\add*. \add ≈We simply don't¦208631 know¦208647 what¦208648 to do¦208650, so we're looking to you¦208652 to rescue us\add*.”
\p
\v 13 \add At that time,\add* all¦208655 of Yehudah¦208657 (men, women, and¦208665 children¦208665) were standing¦208658 \add ≈in¦208659 front¦208659 of\add* Yahweh¦208660,
\v 14 and Yahweh's¦208689 spirit¦208688 came on Yahaziel. (Yahaziel was the son of Zekaryah¦208671, son of Benayah¦208674, son of Yeiel¦208677, son of Mattanyah¦208680 the Levite¦208681, and a descendant¦208684 of Asaf¦208685.) In¦208690 the middle¦208690 of the assembly¦208691
\v 15 he¦208693 said¦208693, “\add ≈Pay¦208694\add* attention¦208694, all of Yehudah¦208697, inhabitants¦208698 of Yerushalem¦208699, and King¦208700 Yehoshafat¦208701. Yahweh¦208705 has this to say to you all, ‘Don't¦208708 be afraid¦208710, and don't¦208708 be dismayed¦208713 by this \add ≈huge¦208716 force\add*, because¦208718 it's not¦208719 your battle¦208721, but¦208693 God's¦208695.\x + \xo 20:15-17: \xt Deu 20:1-4.\x*
\v 16 Tomorrow¦208725, go¦208726 down¦208726 against¦208727 them. Listen, they're coming¦208729 uphill near the Ascent¦208730 of Tsits, and¦208732 you'll find¦208732 them at¦208730 the end¦208734 of the valley¦208735, facing the Yeruel¦208738 wilderness¦208737.
\v 17 You won't¦208754 \add need\add* to fight¦208742 \add ≈them—just take¦208744 your positions, people from Yerushalem¦208753 and wider Yehudah¦208752, and watch Yahweh save you\add*. Don't¦208754 \add ≈be afraid¦208756 or discouraged¦208759\add*. Go¦208761 out¦208761 \add ≈there\add* tomorrow¦208760 and Yahweh will¦208764 be with¦208743 you.’ ”\x + \xo 20:17: \xt Exo 14:13-14.\x*
\p
\v 18 Then¦208766 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208767 bowed¦208766 with his face¦208768 to the ground¦208769, and all¦208770 \add the people from\add* Yerushalem¦208774 and across Yehudah¦208772 fell¦208775 \add to their knees\add* in¦208776 front¦208776 of¦208776 Yahweh¦208777 to worship¦208778 \add *him\add*.
\v 19 Then¦208781 \add some of\add* the Levites¦208782 who were descendants of Kohat and¦208787 Korah stood¦208781 up to \add ≈loudly\add* praise¦208791 Yisrael's¦208794 god¦208793 Yahweh¦208792.
\p
\v 20 They¦208799 rose¦208799 early¦208799 the \add next\add* morning¦208800 and went¦208801 out to¦208802 the Tekoa¦208803 wilderness¦208802, and \add ≈as they¦208804 were leaving\add*, Yehoshafat¦208806 stood¦208805 and \add ≈called out\add*, “Hear me¦208808, inhabitants¦208810 of Yerushalem¦208811 and Yehudah¦208809. Believe in¦208800 \add ≈our\add* god¦208814 Yahweh¦208813, and be¦208815 \add ≈confident\add*. Believe his¦208817 prophets¦208817 and succeed¦208818.”
\v 21 Then¦208820 he consulted¦208820 with¦208831 the people¦208823, and he appointed¦208824 some to sing¦208825 to Yahweh and some to praise¦208827 \add ≈him for his splendour¦208828 and sinlessness\add* as they went¦208831 out¦208831 in¦208832 front¦208832 of¦208832 the \add enemy\add* army, and they were¦208834 saying¦208834, “Give¦208835 thanks¦208835 to Yahweh, because¦208837 his loyal¦208839 commitment \add endures\add* forever¦208838.”
\p
\v 22 As they began¦208842 to sing and praise¦208844 Yahweh¦208846, he¦208845 sent ambushers¦208848 against¦208858 the¦208851 \add ≈Ammonites, Moavites, and Edomites\add* who¦208857 were attacking Yehudah¦208858, and they were defeated¦208859.
\v 23 Then¦208861 the \add ≈Ammonites and Moavites turned on¦208874 the Edomites and completely annihilated¦208872 them¦208872\add*, and \add ≈after that\add* they \add ≈slaughtered each¦208877 other\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈When¦208882 Yehudah's men arrived at the place overlooking the wilderness¦208887, wow¦208892, they¦208892 saw corpses¦208893 all over the ground\add*. No one had escaped¦208897.
\p
\v 25 Then¦208899 Yehoshafat¦208900 and his¦208901 people¦208901 went¦208899 to plunder the spoils, and they¦208906 found¦208906 lots of¦208911 goods¦208909 among¦208907 them¦208907, as well as clothing,\f + \fr 20:25 \ft The Hebrew ‘bodies/corpses’ seems wrong here.\f* and valuable items. They¦208913 took that for¦208914 themselves \add ≈until¦208915 there was nothing left to\add* carry¦208916 away—there was \add ≈so much¦208925 plunder that it took three¦208919 days¦208918 to collect it all\add*.
\v 26 On¦208929 the fourth¦208930 day, they¦208931 assembled¦208931 in¦208929 Berakah Valley and¦208929 praised Yahweh¦208940 there¦208936. That's¦208949 why it's called¦208944 Berakah Valley \add (which means ‘praise/blessing’)\add* to this day.
\v 27 Then¦208956 all the¦208959 men from Yerushalem and¦208956 \add across\add* Yehudah¦208960 returned¦208956 to Yerushalem with¦208963 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208962 \add ≈leading them\add*—celebrating because¦208969 Yahweh¦208972 had¦208971 enabled them to defeat their¦208973 enemies¦208973.
\v 28 \add ≈When¦208983\add* they arrived at¦208977 Yerushalem¦208976, they went¦208975 to¦208980 the¦208982 \add ≈temple\add*, \add playing\add* harps¦208977, lutes, and¦208975 trumpets¦208979.
\v 29 The¦208986 nearby kingdoms¦208991 \add ≈were all¦208989 very afraid of\add* God¦208987 when¦208993 they¦208993 heard¦208993 that¦208994 Yahweh¦208996 had¦208995 fought¦208995 against¦208993 Yisrael's¦208999 enemies¦208998,
\v 30 \add ≈so\add* Yehoshafat's¦209003 kingdom¦209002 was¦209001 untroubled, and¦209004 his god¦209006 gave¦209004 him \add ≈peace¦209001 from all his neighbours\add*.
\s1 The end of Yehoshafat's kingdom
\rem /s1 The End of Jehoshaphat's Reign; Summary of Jehoshaphat's Reign
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 22:41-50)
\p
\v 31 Yehoshafat¦209011 was thirty-five¦209017 \add ≈years old\add* when¦209020 he became¦209020 king¦209020, and he reigned¦209024 over Yehudah¦209014 from Yerushalem¦209025 for twenty-five¦209021 years. His¦209027 mother¦209027 was Shilhi's¦209031 daughter¦209029, Azuvah¦209028.
\v 32 He¦209033 \add ≈had similar priorities to his¦209035 father¦209035 Asa¦209036, doing¦209041 what pleased\add* Yahweh¦209044, and¦209033 he¦209039 didn't¦209037 \add ≈deviate\add* from¦209040 that.
\v 33 \add However,\add* he never removed¦209050 the hilltop¦209047 shrines¦209047, and¦209051 the people¦209052 \add ≈weren't really serious about¦209056 obeying their¦209056 ancestors'¦209058 god¦209057\add*.
\p
\v 34 \add ≈Everything¦209065 else that¦209072 Yehoshafat¦209062 did, from the beginning to the end\add* \add of his reign\add*, was¦209073 written¦209066 down by Hanani's¦209071 son¦209069 Yehu¦209068 in¦209067 the scroll¦209076 about¦209060 Yisrael's¦209078 kings¦209077.
\p
\v 35 \add ≈Later on,\add* Yehudah's¦209087 King Yehoshafat¦209084 \add ≈made¦209083 an alliance¦209083\add* with¦209088 Yisrael's¦209092 King Ahazyah¦209089 (which was a wicked¦209094 thing to do¦209095),
\v 36 and¦209097 they¦209103 worked together to make¦209103 ships¦209104 at¦209105 Etsyon-Gever to sail to Tarshish¦209102.
\v 37 Then¦209108 Dodavahu's¦209112 son¦209110 Eliezer¦209109 from¦209113 Mareshah¦209113 prophesied¦209108 against Yehoshafat¦209116, saying¦209117, “When¦209108 you¦209118 allied yourself with Ahazyah¦209121, Yahweh¦209123 \add ≈destroyed¦209127 what you created\add*.” \add ≈In due course,\add* the ships¦209128 were¦209127 damaged and¦209108 unable to \add ≈sail\add* to Tarshish¦209134.
\c 21
\rem /s1 Jehoram Rules in Judah; Jehoram's Reign
\p
\v 1 Then¦209136 Yehoshafat¦209137 \add ≈died and was¦209141 buried¦209141 with¦209145 his ancestors¦209140\add* in¦209145 ‘The¦209145 City¦209145 of¦209145 David¦209146’, and his son¦209149 Yehoram¦209148 \add !(Jehoram¦209148)\add* \add ≈replaced him¦209150 as king¦209147\add*.
\s1 Yehudah's King Yehoram
\rem /s1 King Jehoram of Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 8:17-24)
\p
\v 2 \add @Yehoram's\add* \add younger\add* brothers¦209154 were¦209166 Azaryah, Yehiel¦209158, Zekaryah¦209159, Azaryah, Mikael¦209161, and¦209152 Shefatyah¦209162,
\v 3 and their¦209175 father¦209175 gave¦209172 them¦209173 many gifts¦209176 of gold¦209179 and silver¦209178 and precious things, along with¦209185 fortified¦209184 cities¦209183 in¦209185 Yehudah¦209185, \add ≈however\add* he \add ≈handed\add* the kingdom¦209188 over to¦209190 Yehoram¦209190 because¦209191 he was¦209194 the oldest \add son\add*.
\rem /s1 Jehoram King of Judah
\v 4 \add ≈After Yehoram¦209198 established firm control\add* of his father's¦209202 kingdom¦209201, he had all¦209207 his brothers¦209209 killed¦209204, as well as some¦209212 of Yisrael's¦209213 leaders¦209212.
\p
\v 5 Yehoram¦209220 was¦209215 thirty-two¦209217 \add ≈years old\add* when¦209221 he became¦209221 the king¦209221, and¦209222 he ruled from Yerushalem¦209225 for eight¦209222 years.
\v 6 He¦209227 did \add many of the evil things\add* that Yisrael's¦209231 kings¦209230 had done¦209233, because¦209236 \add ≈he married one\add* of \add King\add* Ahav's¦209235 daughters¦209237 and¦209227 did things that Yahweh¦209246 \add ≈had said\add* were evil.
\v 7 \add ≈Despite that¦209259,\add* Yahweh¦209251 wouldn't \add ≈eliminate\add* David's¦209256 descendants¦209267, because of the¦209258 \add ≈promise he'd made¦209260\add* with David to ‘keep his¦209267 lamp¦209266 burning’ forever.\x + \xo 21:7: \xt 1Ki 11:36.\x*
\rem /s1 Revolt of Edom
\p
\v 8 \add Meanwhile, Edom had been\add* under¦209275 Yehudah's¦209278 control, but¦209279 \add ≈during Yehoram's reign\add* they¦209279 rebelled¦209273 and¦209279 \add ≈appointed their¦209280 own\add* king.\x + \xo 21:8: \xt Gen 27:40.\x*
\v 9 Yehoram¦209284 took his commanders¦209287 and all¦209288 his chariots, and crossed¦209283 \add the Yordan River\add*, then¦209283 \add ≈at nighttime¦209294\add* he attacked the Edomites who'd surrounded him¦209300 and his chariots.\f + \fr 21:9 \ft The meaning of the second half of this sentence is confusing, so other translations might differ.\f*
\v 10 \add ≈However,\add* Edom¦209306 \add successfully\add* rebelled¦209315 against Yehudah's¦209310 \add ≈control\add*, then¦209305 Livnah¦209316 \add ≈also did the same\add*, because¦209321 \add @Yehoram\add* had¦209322 abandoned¦209322 Yahweh¦209325, his¦209320 ancestors'¦209327 god¦209326.
\rem /s1 Elijah's Letter
\v 11 He also built hilltop¦209334 shrines¦209334 around Yehudah, and he caused Yerushalem's¦209341 inhabitants¦209340 to prostitute¦209337 themselves¦209337,\f + \fr 21:11 \ft This sentence is about worship, not physical adultery, so the reference to prostitution most likely refers to idol worship. Also see verse 13 below.\f* and he drove Yehudah away \add from Yahweh\add*.
\p
\v 12 Then¦209371 \add @King Yehoram\add* received a written¦209350 message from¦209351 the¦209352 prophet¦209352 Eliyah¦209351 \add !(Elijah¦209351)\add*: “Your¦209360 father David's¦209359 god¦209358 Yahweh¦209357 says¦209356 that¦209362 you¦209365 \add decided\add* not¦209363 to¦209353 \add ≈follow\add* your¦209360 father Yehoshafat's¦209367 example, or \add good\add* King Asa's¦209370,
\v 13 but¦209375 rather you \add ≈imitated the behaviour of\add* Yisrael's¦209378 king, so because of that, \add ≈you've caused\add* Yerushalem's¦209386 inhabitants¦209385, as well as \add wider\add* Yehudah¦209382, to commit adultery like Ahav's¦209389 \add ≈family did\add*. Also¦209375, you've killed¦209399 \add ≈your¦209393 own blood brothers¦209393\add*—people who were better¦209397 than¦209398 you.
\v 14 \add ≈So listen, now\add* Yahweh¦209402 is¦209403 going to¦209403 severely afflict¦209403 your people¦209406, including¦209407 your sons¦209407 and¦209408 your wives¦209408, as well as all¦209409 your possessions¦209411,
\v 15 and¦209413 you yourself will \add ≈get an intestinal disease that'll get worse every day until¦209418 your¦209421 innards\add* fall out¦209420.”
\p
\v 16 Then¦209430 Yahweh¦209431 stirred¦209430 the Philistines¦209437 up against Yehoram¦209434, as well as the Arabs¦209438 who¦209439 \add ≈lived beside\add* the Kushites¦209443,
\v 17 and they attacked Yehudah¦209446. They \add ≈did a lot of damage\add* and took away everything valuable from the king's¦209456 palace. They also¦209457 took his wives¦209460 and sons¦209459, other than Yehoahaz¦209469, his youngest¦209470 son¦209465.
\rem /s1 Disease and Death of Jehoram
\p
\v 18 After¦209473 that, Yahweh¦209478 caused an intestinal disease¦209481 in¦209480 Yehoram that couldn't be cured,
\v 19 and it \add ≈progressed day after day until, after two¦209493 years¦209492, his intestines fell out¦209494, and he¦209499 died¦209499 in a lot of¦209506 pain\add*. His people¦209506 didn't¦209502 make¦209504 a \add ≈bonfire in his honour\add* like¦209508 they'd done for his ancestors¦209509.
\p
\v 20 \add @Yehoram\add* was thirty-two¦209513 when he became¦209516 king¦209516, and he ruled from Yerushalem¦209520 for eight¦209517 years¦209518. No one regretted it when he died, and his body was buried¦209524 in ‘The¦209525 City¦209525 of¦209525 David¦209526’, but¦209514 not¦209527 in the \add ≈royal tombs¦209528\add*.
\c 22
\s1 Yehudah's king Ahazyah
\rem /s1 Ahaziah's Reign; Ahaziah Rules in Judah; King Ahaziah of Judah; Ahaziah King of Judah
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (2 Kgs 8:25-29; 9:21-28)
\p
\v 1 The¦209532 inhabitants¦209532 of Yerushalem¦209533 made¦209531 his youngest son Ahazyah\f + \fr 22:1 \ft Called Yehoahaz in 21:17 above. (Replace ‘Yeho’ at the front with ‘Yah’ at the end—the meaning ‘Yahweh has held’ remains the same.)\f* king in his place¦209539, because¦209540 all¦209541 \add ≈his older¦209543 brothers had¦209544 been killed¦209544 by the Arab¦209547 invaders\add*. \add ≈So¦209531\add* Yehoram's¦209553 son Ahazyah reigned¦209549 as Yehudah's¦209555 king.
\v 2 \add *He\add* was twenty-two\f + \fr 22:2 \ft The Hebrew has forty-two here, but we've corrected it from 2 Kgs 8:26.\f* when¦209564 he became¦209564 king¦209564, and¦209565 he reigned¦209567 from Yerushalem¦209568 for one year¦209565. His¦209570 mother¦209570 was Atalyah¦209571, a \add ≈granddaughter\add* of¦209572 Yisrael's \add King\add* Omri¦209574.
\v 3 \add @King Ahazyah\add* \add ≈behaved just like\add* \add King\add* Ahav's¦209582 family had done, because¦209583 his mother¦209584 \add ≈gave him evil advice\add*,
\v 4 \add ≈so\add* he¦209589 did \add ≈what Yahweh¦209592 had said was evil¦209590\add*, just like¦209593 Ahav's¦209594 family, because¦209595 after¦209602 his¦209604 father's¦209604 death¦209603, they'd become \add @Ahazyah's\add* advisors, \add ≈giving destructive¦209605 suggestions\add*.
\v 5 He¦209610 \add ≈followed their¦209609 advice and¦209611 joined\add* \add King\add* Yehoram (son¦209615 of Yisrael's¦209619 King Ahav¦209617) to fight against Aram's¦209626 King Hazael¦209623 at¦209609 Ramot¦209627-Gilead, where Yehoram was wounded¦209629 by the¦209630 Arameans¦209626.
\v 6 Yehoram¦209652 returned¦209635 to Yizreel to recover, because¦209638 he'd been wounded¦209639 at¦209637 Ramah¦209642 in¦209637 the battle against Aram's¦209648 King Hazael¦209646. So¦209635 Yehudah's¦209654 King Ahazyah¦209649 went¦209655 \add ≈up\add* to Yizreel to see¦209656 Yehoram.
\p
\v 7 God¦209669 \add ≈caused Ahazyah's¦209672 downfall¦209671 through\add* his visit to Yehoram. When¦209669 \add @Ahazyah\add* arrived, he went¦209677 with¦209677 Yehoram to meet Nimshi's¦209687 son¦209685 Yehu¦209684, who Yahweh¦209690 had¦209689 appointed to kill¦209691 all of¦209694 Ahav's¦209695 descendants.
\v 8 \add ≈While¦209713 Yehu¦209699 was executing¦209698 judgement¦209698 on Ahav's¦209703 descendants\add*, he discovered Yehudah's¦209708 officials¦209707 there, including¦209704 Ahazyah's¦209711 nephews who'd been serving¦209712 him, and¦209697 he killed¦209714 \add all of\add* them¦209714 \add as well\add*.
\v 9 Then¦209716 Yehu went searching for Ahazyah and found him hiding¦209722 in¦209723 Shomron¦209723 \add !(Samaria¦209723) city\add*. They captured¦209720 him and took him to Yehu, and killed him. They did bury¦209729 him, because¦209730 they¦209731 said¦209731, “He was¦209732 \add ≈the¦209732 grandson\add* of \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦209734 who \add ≈tried hard to please\add* Yahweh¦209741.” \add ≈After¦209741 that,\add* there¦209745 were no \add ≈descendants of Ahazyah who were powerful enough to become Yehudah's king\add*.
\s1 Yehudah's queen Atalyah
\rem /s1 Athaliah Rules in Judah; Athaliah Seizes the Throne; Queen Athaliah of Judah; Athaliah and Joash
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 11:1-3)
\p
\v 10 \add ≈When¦209752\add* Ahazyah's¦209754 mother¦209753 Atalyah found out that¦209756 her¦209758 son¦209758 had died¦209757, she¦209755 \add ≈took action\add* and¦209752 destroyed¦209760 all¦209763 \add ≈his family members who could become king\add* of Yehudah¦209768.
\v 11 \add ≈However, a princess named\add* Yehoshaveat took¦209770 Ahazyah's son¦209778 Yoash¦209777, and she \add ≈sneaked him away from among¦209783\add* the king's¦209786 sons¦209784 who¦209787 were¦209787 about¦209787 to be¦209787 killed, and she hid him and his¦209792 nurse¦209792 in¦209793 a bedroom. Yehoshaveat was the daughter¦209797 of \add the late\add* King¦209774 Yehoram¦209800 and the wife¦209801 of Yehoyada¦209802 the priest¦209803 (she was Ahazyah's sister¦209807), \add and she\add* hid \add @Yoash\add* from Atalyah¦209810 \add ≈so she couldn't\add* kill him.
\v 12 He¦209814 \add ≈stayed in hiding¦209818 with¦209815 them¦209815 in the¦209817 temple\add* for six¦209819 years¦209820 \add ≈while\add* Atalyah¦209821 ruled over¦209823 \add ≈Yehudah¦209817\add*.
\c 23
\s1 Revolt against queen Atalyah
\rem /s1 Revolt against Athaliah; The Revolt against Athaliah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 11:4-16)
\p
\v 1 \add ≈The following year¦209828\add*, \add the priest\add* Yehoyada¦209831 \add ≈took¦209832 courage\add* and made an agreement¦209862 with¦209828 the commanders¦209835 of units of a hundred¦209836 \add soldiers\add*: Azaryah (Yehoram's son), Yishmael¦209841 (Yehohanan's¦209844 son), \add another\add* Azaryah (Oved's¦209848 son), Maaseyah¦209851 (Adayah's¦209854 son), and Elishafat¦209857 (Zikri's¦209860 son).
\v 2 They¦209864 went¦209864 throughout Yehudah¦209865 and gathered¦209866 all the Levites¦209869 and the \add ≈clan leaders\add* from all the cities¦209872. \add ≈When¦209864\add* they¦209877 came¦209877 to¦209878 Yerushalem¦209880,
