\v 8 \add ≈So¦209979\add* the Levites¦209980 and¦209979 the other people did \add ≈everything\add* Yehoyada the priest¦209989 had¦209987 instructed¦209987. Each¦209991 \add leader\add* took¦209990 his¦209994 men¦209994, both those¦209998 starting duty¦210002 on the Rest Day, as well as the others \add ≈finishing their duties that day\add*, because¦210000 Yehoyada \add ≈didn't¦210001 dismiss any of the groups\add*.
\v 9 Then¦210009 Yehoyada¦210010 the priest¦210011 gave¦210009 each of¦210012 those commanders¦210012 the spears¦210016, and the large and small¦210022 shields¦210022 which \add ≈had been put in the temple by\add* King¦210024 David¦210025.
\v 10 He¦210030 stationed¦210030 all the people¦210035, each¦210036 one holding their weapon¦210038, \add ≈right¦210042 across the end of the temple\add*, around the altar¦210048 and the \add ≈temple\add*, and all around the king¦210052.
\v 11 Then they¦210055 brought¦210055 out¦210055 \add ≈young Yoash\add*, put¦210061 a crown¦210065 on \add ≈his head\add*, gave him \add ≈a scroll with the agreement on it¦210070\add*, and proclaimed him as king. Then Yehoyada¦210072 and his sons¦210073 anointed¦210071 him \add with olive oil\add* and shouted, “\add Long\add* live¦210075 the king!”
