\v 12 \add ≈When¦210095\add* Atalyah¦210080 heard¦210079 the sound¦210083 of¦210083 people running¦210085, and¦210086 \add ≡people\add* praising¦210086 the king¦210089, she¦210090 went¦210090 to¦210091 the \add ≈temple\add*
\v 13 to look, and wow, the \add young\add* king¦210099 was¦210100 standing¦210100 \add where previous kings had stood\add* by the pillar¦210103 at¦210104 the \add temple\add* entrance¦210104, with the commanders and trumpeters¦210106 beside him. The people¦210112 were all \add ≈cheering\add* and blowing¦210115 trumpets¦210116, and singers¦210117 with instruments¦210118 were leading¦210120 the praise¦210121. Then¦210097 Atalyah¦210123 tore¦210122 her¦210126 robe and \add ≈shouted out\add*, “Treason! Treason!”
