\v 16 Then Yehoyada¦210178 \add the priest\add* \add ≈got the people¦210184 to formally agree that they and¦210185 the king¦210186 would be¦210187 loyal to\add* Yahweh¦210189,
\v 17 \add ≈so\add* all¦210192 the people¦210194 went¦210191 to Baal's \add ≈temple\add* and tore it¦210198 down. They smashed its altars and idols, and killed¦210210 Baal's priest¦210208 Mattan¦210207 in¦210211 front¦210211 of¦210211 the altars.
\v 18 Then¦210214 Yehoyada¦210215 \add ≈created the roster\add* for the temple \add duties of\add* the priests¦210220 and¦210236 Levites¦210221 that \add King\add* David¦210224 had¦210223 \add previously\add* assigned¦210223, \add including\add* offering¦210229 burnt¦210230 offerings¦210230 to¦210229 Yahweh¦210218 with¦210219 happiness and singing¦210236, \add ≈following\add* Mosheh's¦210234 written¦210232 instructions.
\v 19 He¦210247 \add ≈also\add* stationed¦210241 guards at¦210243 the \add ≈temple\add* gates¦210245 so that no one could enter if they were \add ≈ceremonially ‘unclean¦210251’\add*.
\p
\v 20 Then¦210256 \add @Yehoyada\add* took¦210256 those commanders¦210259, and the nobles¦210263 and leaders¦210266, and all the people, and \add #they\add* brought¦210274 the king¦210277 \add ≈out of the temple\add* and down into the palace through the Upper Gate, and sat¦210287 him on¦210267 the royal¦210293 throne¦210292.
\v 21 Then¦210295 all¦210296 of Yehudah's people¦210298 \add ≈celebrated\add*, and then¦210295 the¦210301 city¦210301 was¦210302 \add ≈peaceful¦210302 and quiet\add*, as Atalyah¦210305 had¦210306 been put¦210306 to¦210306 death¦210306 with¦210307 a sword¦210307.
\c 24
\s1 Yehudah's king Yoash
\rem /s1 King Joash of Judah; Joash Repairs the Temple
