\v 4 \add ≈Sometime later,\add* Yoash¦210355 \add ≈decided it would be good\add* to¦210356 repair Yahweh's¦210360 residence,
\v 5 and he¦210362 gathered¦210362 the priests¦210365 and Levites, and told them¦210368, “Go¦210369 out¦210369 to Yehudah's¦210371 cities¦210370 and collect¦210372 enough money¦210376 \add ≈across the country\add* to \add ≈renovate\add* God's¦210382 house¦210381 \add ≈in¦210385 the next few years\add*. \add ≈Make this a priority\add*.” \add ≈But¦210362\add* the Levites didn't¦210389 \add ≈get on¦210385 to it\add*,
\v 6 \add ≈so\add* \add @the king¦210394\add* summoned Yehoyada¦210395 and \add ≈demanded\add*, “Why¦210399 haven't you¦210402 \add ≈followed up on¦210403 sending\add* the Levites¦210405 throughout Yerushalem¦210408 and \add across\add* Yehudah¦210407 \add ≈to collect the annual tax¦210411 instituted\add* by Yahweh's¦210415 servant¦210413 Mosheh¦210412 \add !(Moses¦210412)\add* \add ≈for the people to contribute to the costs of¦210418 the sacred tent¦210418\add*?”\x + \xo 24:6: \xt Exo 30:11-16.\x*
\p
\v 7 (The¦210423 wicked¦210423 Atalyah's¦210422 people had¦210425 \add previously\add* broken¦210425 into¦210425 Yahweh's residence and¦210430 \add taken\add* some of the sacred¦210433 items from Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add* to use for¦210438 Baal¦210438 \add worship\add*.)
\p
\v 8 The¦210449 king¦210441 ordered that a chest¦210443 be made¦210442 and¦210440 placed outside¦210450 the \add main\add* \add ≈temple\add* entrance.
\v 9 They¦210452 made¦210452 an announcement in Yerushalem¦210456 and¦210456 \add throughout\add* Yehudah¦210455 that people were to bring¦210457 to Yahweh¦210458 the \add ≈tax¦210459 that was instituted\add* by God's servant¦210461 Mosheh¦210460 \add ≈when they¦210452 were still\add* in the wilderness¦210467.
\v 10 All¦210470 the officials¦210472 and the people¦210475 agreed \add with this policy, so\add* they¦210476 brought¦210476 \add >their contributions\add* and dropped¦210477 them into the chest¦210478 until¦210479 it filled up.
\v 11 Every day, when¦210485 the Levites¦210494 who'd been given oversight¦210491 over the chest¦210488 by¦210493 the king saw¦210495 that¦210496 it was¦210498 full, they'd \add ≈fetch\add* one of the king's¦210502 secretaries along with¦210484 one of the head¦210505 priest's¦210504 officials¦210503, and they'd empty¦210506 the box and return¦210511 it to its¦210514 place¦210514, so¦210515 they amassed \add ≈a large sum of\add* money¦210522.
\p
\v 12 The¦210526 king¦210526 and Yehoyada¦210527 \add the priest\add* gave¦210525 \add @the collected funds\add* to the people who worked¦210544 on the \add ≈temple renovations\add*. They¦210536 \add used them\add* to hire stone-workers¦210538 and \add ≈carpenters¦210539\add* to restore¦210540 the \add ≈temple building\add*, as well as for iron and bronze¦210546 craftsmen.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦210553\add* they¦210553 \add ≈started on¦210559 the work\add*, and the \add ≈temple restoration¦210560 went¦210556 ahead\add*. They¦210564 rebuilt the \add ≈temple following\add* its¦210567 \add original\add* specifications¦210567, and strengthened¦210568 it¦210568.
\v 14 Whey they'd finished¦210570, they brought¦210571 the remainder¦210577 of the funds \add back\add* to the king¦210573 and Yehoyada, and they made¦210579 items for \add ≈the temple\add*, items \add ≈used in\add* ministry and for burnt offerings¦210593, and dishes¦210587 and gold¦210589 and silver¦210590 items. During Yehoyada's¦210574 \add ≈time¦210599\add*, they were¦210591 offering¦210592 regular burnt sacrifices in Yahweh's¦210583 \add ≈temple\add*.
