\v 17 After¦210632 Yehoyada's¦210634 death¦210633, Yehudah's¦210637 leaders¦210636 went¦210635 to \add young King\add* Yoash and \add ≈declared their loyalty\add* to \add *him\add*, and \add *he¦210641\add* listened¦210641 to them¦210643.
\v 18 Then¦210645 they abandoned¦210645 the \add ≈temple\add* of their ancestors' god¦210650 Yahweh¦210649, and they \add ≈worshipped\add* the Asherah¦210655 \add poles\add* and idols¦210658, and \add God\add* was¦210659 angry at¦210666 Yerushalem¦210665 and Yehudah¦210664 because of their \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\v 19 He¦210675 sent¦210669 prophets¦210671 to \add tell them\add* to return back¦210672 to \add *him\add*, and¦210669 \add although\add* they warned¦210676 \add @the people\add*, \add @the people\add* didn't¦210678 \add ≈take any notice\add*.
