\v 20 Then God's¦210683 spirit¦210682 \add ≈enveloped\add* Zekaryah¦210687, the son¦210688 of¦210688 Yehoyada¦210690 the priest¦210691, and he stood¦210692 \add ≈up\add* and told the people¦210694, “God \add ≈asks\add* why¦210701 you \add people\add* are¦210702 \add ≈violating\add* \add *his\add* commands¦210706. Because¦210710 you abandoned Yahweh¦210707, he's¦210716 abandoned you \add people\add*.”\x + \xo 24:20-21: \xt Mat 23:35; Luk 11:51.\x*
\v 21 \add ≈However¦210727,\add* \add @the people\add* conspired¦210719 against \add @Zekaryah\add*, and¦210719 the king¦210724 ordered him to be \add ≈executed by\add* stoning him in¦210723 the \add ≈temple\add* courtyard¦210725.
\v 22 King¦210733 Yoash¦210732 \add ≈disregarded\add* the loyal¦210734 commitment that¦210735 Yehoyada¦210737 had¦210736 shown to his father¦210738, and killed¦210740 his son¦210743. As¦210744 \add @Zekaryah\add* was dying¦210744, he said¦210745, “Yahweh¦210747 will see¦210746 \add >this\add* and \add find a way to\add* avenge¦210748.”
