\v 5 so they¦213405 \add ≈sent messages¦213382 across\add* all¦213385 of Yisrael \add and Yehudah\add*, from Beer¦213388-Sheva \add in the south\add* to Dan¦213393 \add in the far north\add*, for¦213395 \add the people\add* to come¦213394 to Yerushalem¦213401 to \add ≈celebrate\add* the Passover¦213396 \add to honour\add* Yisrael's¦213387 god¦213398 Yahweh¦213397. (They¦213405 hadn't previously been observing the written¦213406 instructions.)
\v 6 Runners¦213409 took the letters¦213410 from the king and his¦213413 officials¦213413, \add going\add* to all of Yisrael and Yehudah¦213417 with¦213410 the king's¦213419 command¦213418: “Descendants of Yisrael, return to Yahweh¦213427, the god¦213428 of Abraham¦213429, Yitshak¦213430, and Yisrael, and he'll return to you—the \add ≈group that¦213436\add* escaped¦213435 from the \add ≈control\add* of the Assyrian kings¦213439.
\v 7 Don't¦213442 be¦213444 like your fathers¦213445 and¦213442 brothers¦213446 who¦213447 weren't faithful to Yahweh¦213449, their¦213451 ancestors'¦213451 god¦213450, \add provoking him\add* \add ≈to leave them¦213452 decimated, as¦213454 you can see¦213456\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈So don't¦213459 be stubborn\add* like¦213463 your ancestors¦213463 were. \add ≈Obey\add* Yahweh and come¦213468 to¦213469 the sanctuary¦213469 that¦213470 he's¦213471 consecrated¦213471 forever¦213472, and serve¦213473 your god¦213477 Yahweh \add ≈so¦213478 he'll\add* turn¦213478 his anger¦213481 away from¦213479 you.
