\v 26 Everyone in Yerushalem was very happy, because¦213815 nothing like¦213824 that¦213824 had happened in Yerushalem since¦213816 the time¦213816 when David's¦213820 son¦213818 Shelomoh¦213817 \add !(Solomon¦213817)\add* was king¦213821.
\v 27 \add ≈Finally,\add* the priests¦213829 and Levites¦213830 stood up and \add ≈prayed a blessing¦213831 on¦213836\add* the people¦213834, and their voice¦213836 was heard¦213835 because their prayer¦213838 reached \add @God's\add* holy residence in¦213836 the heavens¦213841.
\c 31
\s1 Hizkiyah's religious reforms
