\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 When that was all over, all \add those\add* Israelis¦213879 went¦213848 out¦213848 to Yehudah's¦213855 cities and shattered the pillars¦213857 and cut¦213858 down the Asherah¦213859 poles¦213859, and they tore down the hilltop¦213863 shrines¦213863 and altars¦213866 from the entire¦213845 Yehudah-Benyamin¦213870 \add region\add*, and also up in¦213871 the Efrayim¦213871-Menashsheh¦213872 \add region\add*. Once they'd finished¦213844 that, they all returned¦213876 to their¦213883 own¦213882 land and cities.
\rem /s1 Contributions for Worship
\p
\v 2 \add King\add* Hizkiyah¦213887 allocated the priests¦213891 and Levites¦213892 \add into\add* divisions¦213895 for the various different types of duties: for doing burnt¦213902 offerings and peace¦213903 offerings, for other services¦213899, and for thanksgiving¦213905 and praise¦213906 at¦213907 the \add ≈temple\add* gates¦213907.
\v 3 The king¦213913 \add ≈contributed¦213912 some of his¦213916 own¦213916 funds\add* for burnt offerings \add to be sacrificed\add* each morning¦213919 and evening¦213920, as well as for the Rest Days and the New Moon celebrations, and on¦213926 the other special days as per the written¦213925 instructions \add ≈that had come from\add* Yahweh¦213927.\x + \xo 31:3: \xt Num 28:1–29:39.\x*
\p
\v 4 He¦213929 told the people¦213930 \add ≈living in¦213939\add* Yerushalem¦213932 to give¦213933 the \add prescribed\add* \add #portions¦213934\add* to the priests¦213935 and¦213936 Levites¦213936, so¦213937 that¦213937 they¦213938 could¦213938 \add ≈focus on¦213939 serving\add* Yahweh¦213940,\x + \xo 31:4-5: \xt Num 18:12-13,21.\x*
\v 5 and as soon as the message¦213943 reached them, the Israelis¦213947 \add started\add* giving the first¦213948 portions of \add their harvests of\add* grain¦213949, new¦213950 wine¦213950, oil¦213951, and honey¦213952, and of all the produce¦213954 from the countryside¦213955, so they brought¦213959 a tenth of \add the harvests of\add* all their crops.
\v 6 The¦213961 people from Yisrael¦213962 and Yehudah \add ≈who¦213964 were¦213964 living¦213964 in¦213965\add* Yehudah's¦213966 cities¦213965 also¦213967 \add ≈brought¦213978 a tenth\add* of¦213970 their cattle and sheep¦213972, as well as a sacred¦213974 tenth consecrated¦213975 to¦213976 their god¦213977 Yahweh¦213976, and it was all put in big piles.
\v 7 That all began¦213986 in¦213984 \add ≈May\add* and¦213989 was finished¦213991 by \add ≈September\add*,
\v 8 and \add when King\add* Hizkiyah¦213995 and \add &his\add* officials¦213996 came¦213994 and saw¦213997 the¦214000 piles, they¦214001 \add ≈praised\add* Yahweh¦214004 and his \add ≈Israeli\add* people¦214006.
\v 9 \add ≈When\add* Hizkiyah¦214011 asked the priests¦214014 and¦214015 Levites¦214015 about the piles,
\v 10 Azaryah¦214022 the chief¦214024 priest¦214023 (a descendant of¦214026 Tsadok¦214026) told him, “\add ≈Since¦214041 the people started¦214028 bringing¦214030 their contributions¦214029\add* to¦214030 the \add ≈temple\add*, we've¦214034 been¦214035 eating¦214034 well, and even had¦214036 left-overs, because¦214040 Yahweh¦214033 has¦214042 blessed¦214042 his people, and \add ≈all this is¦214046 the remainder¦214046\add*.”
