\p
\v 29 Then the king¦216021 summoned all¦216025 the elders¦216027 from Yerushalem¦216029 and¦216029 \add ≈from across\add* Yehudah¦216028,
\v 30 and they all \add ≈walked\add* up to the \add ≈temple\add*, with¦216052 the inhabitants¦216040 of Yerushalem¦216041 and \add all of\add* Yehudah¦216039, and the priests¦216042 and the Levites¦216043, and all the people¦216046, \add ≈irrespective of their¦216052 standing in the community\add*. Then¦216031 \add @the king¦216032\add* read everything out to them that was on¦216052 the Torah scroll¦216058 that had¦216060 been¦216060 found¦216060 in the \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 31 Then¦216064 the king¦216065 stood¦216064 at¦216066 his \add normal\add* place¦216068 and \add ≈made¦216069 an agreement¦216072\add* with Yahweh: to obey Yahweh and follow his instructions¦216083 and his regulations¦216083 and statutes, \add ≈sincerely and with all¦216087 his energy\add*—doing¦216090 what was in the \add ≈joint understanding\add* that¦216095 had been written¦216095 on¦216096 the scroll¦216098.
\v 32 Then¦216101 he¦216101 had everyone¦216103 from Yerushalem and Benyamin¦216107 take a stand¦216101 \add in agreement to it\add*, and \add so\add* Yerushalem's¦216106 inhabitants¦216109 \add ≈renewed\add* their agreement with¦216106 their ancestors'¦216114 god.
\v 33 \add ≈So¦216116\add* \add King\add* Yoshiyah¦216117 removed¦216116 all the disgusting \add idols\add* from \add ≈all the Israeli¦216127 regions\add*, and¦216116 he¦216129 \add ≈made¦216129\add* everyone¦216131 in¦216134 Yisrael¦216128 serve¦216135 their god Yahweh—\add ≈during his¦216142 lifetime\add* they¦216144 never turned¦216144 away from Yahweh, their ancestors'¦216148 god.
\c 35
