\p
\v 1 Then \add King\add* Yoshiyah¦216152 \add ≈prepared\add* a ‘pass-over¦216154’ celebration in¦216153 Yerushalem¦216153, and¦216156 they slaughtered¦216156 the \add ≈lambs at¦216153 the end of March\add*.
\v 2 \add *He¦216171\add* assigned the priests¦216164 to \add ≈the various tasks that needed to be done\add*, and¦216168 \add ≈encouraged¦216168 them to do their¦216167 work¦216169 well\add*.
\v 3 He¦216173 told the Levites¦216174 (they'd been \add ≈separated\add* \add from the other tribes\add* in order to serve Yahweh) who were teaching¦216175 all of¦216185 Yisrael, “Place the sacred¦216180 box¦216185 in the house¦216188 that¦216189 was built¦216190 by David's¦216194 son¦216192, Yisrael's¦216179 King¦216195 Shelomoh \add !(Solomon¦216191)\add*—it won't¦216197 be¦216197 a burden¦216200 any more for¦216199 your shoulders¦216201. Now¦216202 serve your god¦216207 Yahweh and¦216173 his¦216209 \add ≈Israeli¦216195\add* people¦216209,
\v 4 and prepare¦216212 yourselves in¦216219 your clan divisions¦216218 as per the¦216215 instructions written by¦216219 Yisrael's¦216222 King¦216221 David¦216220 and his¦216225 son¦216225 Shelomoh¦216224.\x + \xo 35:4: \xt 2Ch 8:14.\x*
