\v 6 Consecrate¦216243 yourselves¦216243 and¦216241 slaughter¦216241 the ‘pass-over¦216242’ \add lambs\add* for \add ≈the people\add* \add ≈as per the instructions\add* \add given\add* through Mosheh¦216252 \add !(Moses¦216252)\add* by Yahweh¦216249.
\p
\v 7 \add King\add* Yoshiyah¦216256 \add ≈provided\add* thirty¦216270 thousand lambs¦216260 and young goats¦216263 from his own flocks¦216259 for¦216257 the ‘pass-over¦216265’ \add sacrifices\add*, and three¦216273 thousand bulls¦216272 \add ≈from his own herds\add*.
\v 8 His officials \add ≈also\add* contributed¦216285 for \add the benefit of\add* the people¦216282, priests, and Levites¦216284. The chief temple officials Hilkiyah¦216286, Zekaryah¦216287, and Yehiel¦216288 donated 2,600 lambs and three¦216299 hundred¦216300 cattle¦216298 to the priests.
\v 9 The Levite¦216311 leaders¦216310 Konanyah and his¦216306 younger brothers¦216306 Shemayah¦216304 and Netanel¦216305, along with Hashavyah¦216307, Yeiel¦216308, and Yozavad¦216309, \add together\add* contributed¦216312 five¦216315 thousand¦216316 lambs and three hundred¦216319 bulls¦216317.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦216321 everything\add* was¦216321 prepared¦216321 as the king¦216333 had commanded¦216332, and the priests¦216324 stood¦216323 at¦216325 their places¦216327, and the Levites¦216328 were there in their \add various\add* divisions¦216331,
\v 11 and¦216335 they¦216335 slaughtered¦216335 the ‘pass-over¦216336’ \add lambs\add*, then¦216335 the priests¦216338 sprinkled¦216337 the blood while the Levites¦216340 skinned¦216341 \add >the animals\add*.
\v 12 They set aside¦216343 \add the animals\add* to be burnt¦216344 \add on the altar\add*, \add ≈in¦216355 order to give¦216345 them¦216345 to the various family groups¦216346 to offer¦216344\add* to Yahweh¦216353, following¦216357 the instructions Mosheh¦216356 had written¦216354 down. They did the same thing with¦216355 the cattle¦216358.
\v 13 They¦216360 roasted¦216360 the ‘pass-over¦216361’ \add meal\add* over the fire¦216362 as per the instructions, and they¦216365 boiled¦216365 the meat of the sacred¦216364 offerings¦216364 in¦216362 pots and kettles¦216367 and pans, and \add ≈served the meat immediately to¦216370 all¦216370 the people¦216373 who were there\add*.\x + \xo 35:13: \xt Exo 12:8-9.\x*
\v 14 Afterwards¦216394, \add @the Levites¦216389\add* prepared¦216376 the meal for themselves and for the priests (Aharon's¦216382 descendants¦216381), because¦216379 the priests had been busy sacrificing the burnt¦216384 offerings¦216383 and the fat portions right through to¦216391 the evening.
\v 15 The singers¦216396 (Asaf's¦216399 descendants¦216397) were¦216400 at¦216400 their posts, as they'd been commanded¦216403 by \add King\add* David¦216404, Asaf, Heyman¦216406, and¦216396 the king's prophet Yedutun¦216407. The \add ≈men guarding the gates didn't¦216414 have to leave their posts\add*, because¦216419 their fellow Levites¦216422 prepared¦216423 \add >food\add* for¦216424 them.\x + \xo 35:15: \xt 1Ch 25:1.\x*
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦216426 on that day¦216431, everything that needed to be done for worshipping Yahweh¦216430 was done\add*. They¦216439 celebrated the ‘pass-over¦216434’ festival, and¦216426 they sacrificed burnt¦216436 offerings¦216436 as King¦216441 Yoshiyah¦216442 had commanded¦216440.
\v 17 The¦216445 \add ≈Israelis¦216445 who¦216448 were¦216448 there celebrated\add* the ‘pass-over¦216451’ that¦216453 \add ≈day\add*, then¦216444 they¦216444 celebrated the ‘Festival¦216456 of¦216456 Flat¦216447 Bread¦216457’ for seven¦216458 days¦216459.\x + \xo 35:17: \xt Exo 12:1-20.\x*
\v 18 There hadn't been a ‘pass-over’ celebration done like that¦216479 in¦216466 Yisrael since¦216467 the \add ≈time¦216467\add* of the prophet¦216469 Shemuel¦216468 \add !(Samuel¦216468)\add*, and none of Yisrael's¦216466 kings¦216472 had¦216477 ever done it like Yoshiyah¦216482 did, along with¦216466 the priests¦216483 and Levites¦216484 and the \add ≈people¦216490\add* from Yerushalem¦216491 and all¦216485 of Yehudah¦216487 and Yisrael.
\v 19 They celebrated that¦216501 \add ≈festival\add* in¦216494 the¦216497 eighteenth¦216494 year¦216496 of¦216498 Yoshiyah's¦216498 reign¦216497.
\s1 The death of Yehudah's King Yoshiyah
