\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 23:28-30)
\p
\v 20 After¦216503 all¦216504 of¦216504 Yoshiyah's¦216509 \add ≈work on temple restoration\add*, Egypt's¦216517 King¦216515 Neko went to attack Karkemish \add city\add* on the¦216522 Euphrates¦216522 river, and¦216523 Yoshiyah went out¦216523 to \add ≈confront\add* him¦216524.
\v 21 \add @Neko\add* sent¦216527 messengers¦216529 to tell \add @Yoshiyah\add*, “What's¦216533 \add ≈this got to do with\add* you, King¦216537 of¦216537 Yehudah¦216538? \add ≈We're not¦216539 attacking you at present\add*, \add ≈because¦216544 we're in a different fight\add*, and God told me to hurry¦216551. \add ≈Don't¦216539 oppose¦216555\add* God, who's¦216556 with me, and don't¦216539 \add make\add* him destroy¦216561 you.”
\v 22 \add ≈However,\add* Yoshiyah¦216566 \add ≈wouldn't listen\add*, but¦216563 disguised¦216573 himself¦216573 \add ≈before going into battle¦216583\add*. He¦216565 didn't¦216563 listen to Neko \add ≈even though he was speaking for\add* God¦216581, so he went¦216582 to fight¦216570 on¦216584 the Megiddon¦216585 plain¦216584.
\p
\v 23 King¦216589 Yoshiyah¦216590 was hit by the archers¦216588, and¦216587 he¦216591 told his¦216593 servants¦216593, “\add ≈Get me¦216594 away¦216594 from here\add*, because¦216595 I'm badly wounded¦216596.”
\v 24 \add ≈So¦216599\add* his servants¦216600 \add ≈lifted him off his\add* chariot and took¦216599 him \add ≈on¦216615 his reserve\add* chariot back to¦216610 Yerushalem, \add where he died\add*. He¦216614 was¦216614 buried¦216614 in¦216615 \add ≈a tomb¦216615 with his ancestors¦216616\add*, and all¦216617 of Yerushalem and Yehudah¦216619 mourned¦216621 over \add *him\add*.
\p
\v 25 \add The prophet\add* Yirmeyah¦216628 \add !(Jeremiah¦216628)\add* wrote¦216651 a \add ≈funeral song\add* for him, which the male¦216635 and¦216637 female¦216637 singers¦216637 still use \add ≈at¦216638 funerals\add* to this day¦216644. \add ≈That became a custom¦216646 in Yisrael¦216649—the words of that song are¦216651 written¦216651 in a scroll of funeral songs\add*.
\p
\v 26 The¦216656 record of¦216656 all the¦216657 other things Yoshiyah¦216658 did \add ≈while he was king\add*, and¦216656 his¦216659 loyal¦216659 commitment \add ≈to following Yahweh's¦216662 instructions\add*,
\v 27 including¦216666 his actions from the beginning to the end \add of his reign\add*, was written¦216668 on¦216669 the scroll¦216671 ‘The¦216672 kings¦216672 of Yisrael¦216674 and¦216664 Yehudah¦216675’.
\c 36
