\v 2 Yehoahaz¦216698 was¦216693 twenty-three¦216696 when¦216699 he became¦216699 king¦216699, and¦216700 he reigned¦216702 from Yerushalem¦216703 for \add only\add* three months¦216701.
\v 3 \add Then\add* Egypt's¦216708 king¦216706 deposed¦216705 him¦216705 and \add ≈forced the country to pay\add* an \add annual\add* tribute of \add ≈thirty kilograms\add* of gold¦216719 and \add ≈three tonnes\add* of silver¦216717.
\v 4 Egypt's¦216724 King¦216722 Neko took¦216742 Yehoahaz¦216740 to Egypt, and then¦216721 the¦216722 king made¦216721 his¦216728 \add younger\add* brother¦216728 Elyakim king over¦216729 Yehudah¦216731 and Yerushalem¦216732, \add ≈although\add* he changed¦216733 Elyakim's¦216727 name¦216736 to Yehoyakim¦216737.\x + \xo 36:4: \xt Jer 22:11-12.\x*
