\v 7 along with¦216783 some¦216776 items from Yahweh's¦216778 \add ≈temple\add* that were taken to Babylon¦216781 and¦216776 placed in¦216783 \add @the king's\add* temple \add *there\add*.
\p
\v 8 The record of all the other things Yehoyakim¦216788 did \add ≈while he was king, including¦216789\add* the disgusting things he did, was written¦216796 on the scroll¦216799 ‘The kings¦216800 of Yisrael¦216801 and Yehudah¦216802’, and his¦216789 son¦216805 Yehoyakin¦216804 \add ≈replaced him¦216806 as king\add*.
