\v 13 \add ≈He'd become very stubborn and wouldn't\add* return to Yisrael's¦216897 god¦216883 Yahweh¦216895, and he¦216888 \add also\add* rebelled¦216880 against¦216892 King¦216878 Nebuchadnezzar¦216879, who'd made¦216888 him¦216882 \add ≈promise in¦216878 front of¦216891 God¦216883\add* \add to be loyal\add*.\x + \xo 36:13: \xt Eze 17:15.\x*
\v 14 \add ≈In addition\add*, all¦216900 the leaders¦216902 of the priests¦216903 and the people¦216904 \add of Yehudah\add* \add ≈became more and more unfaithful¦216906, doing disgusting things often done in other\add* nations¦216913, and then they¦216914 defiled Yahweh's¦216918 residence, which¦216919 he'd consecrated¦216920 in Yerushalem¦216921.
\rem /s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\p
\v 15 \add ≈So¦216923\add* Yahweh¦216924, their¦216926 ancestors'¦216926 god¦216925, \add ≈sent¦216923 many messages via his prophets,\add* because¦216932 he felt compassion¦216934 for his people¦216937 and¦216923 his residence,
\v 16 \add ≈but¦216942\add* they¦216942 mocked¦216948 God's¦216945 messengers¦216944 and¦216942 \add ≈rejected\add* the messages¦216947—ridiculing his prophets¦216949 until Yahweh¦216954 \add ≈became so angry that he couldn't be stopped\add*.
\rem /s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\v 17 \add ≈So¦216961\add* \add Yahweh\add* \add ≈sent\add* the Chaldean king¦216965 against¦216962 them, and \add ≈the Chaldeans¦216966 ran Yehudah's young men through\add* with¦216970 the sword¦216970, \add even\add* in¦216970 the \add ≈temple\add*, and \add #they\add* didn't¦216973 spare any of the young men or women, or \add even\add* those who were older or elderly—\add @God\add* allowed \add @Nebuchadnezzar\add* to \add thoroughly\add* \add ≈defeat them\add*.\x + \xo 36:17: \xt Jer 21:1-10; 34:1-5.\x*
\v 18 Then¦216985 he took \add ≈everything¦216997 valuable\add*, big or small¦216990, from God's temple, as well as from the king¦216995 and¦216985 his¦216996 officials¦216996.
\v 19 They¦217001 \add ≈set God's¦217005 temple on¦217014 fire¦217014\add*, and tore down¦217006 \add some of\add* the wall¦217008 \add surrounding\add* Yerushalem¦217009, burnt all its palaces¦217012, and destroyed¦217019 everything valuable¦217018.\x + \xo 36:19: \xt 1Ki 9:8.\x*
\v 20 \add ≈Anyone else who was still alive\add* was taken¦217022 to Babylon¦217029, where they¦217030 became¦217030 servants¦217034 to \add @the king\add* and¦217033 his¦217033 children until¦217035 \add the time when\add* the Persians \add ≈came to power\add*.
\v 21 \add That\add* fulfilled¦217041 God's message¦217042 that Yirmeyah¦217046 had \add previously proclaimed\add*, that the land¦217050 would become desolate¦217057 \add to make up for\add* the Rest Days¦217056 \add that had been ignored\add*—that took seventy¦217060 years¦217061.\x + \xo 36:21: \xt Jer 25:11; 29:10.\x*
\s1 Cyrus sends the exiles back to Yehudah
\rem /s1 Cyrus Commands the Jews to Return; Cyrus Proclaims Liberty for the Exiles; Cyrus Allows the Exiles to Return
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (Ezra 1:1-4)
\p
\v 22 During the first year¦217064 that King Cyrus \add (Heb. Koresh)\add* reigned over Persia¦217068, in¦217073 order¦217069 to \add further\add* fulfil¦217069 what Yahweh had said¦217093 via \add the prophet\add* Yirmeyah¦217074, Yahweh \add ≈worked on¦217073\add* the spirit¦217079 of King Cyrus who then wrote¦217092 this ruling \add and sent messengers\add* to announce it throughout his¦217089 kingdom¦217089:
\v 23 “I, Persia's¦217102 King¦217101 Cyrus¦217099, declare that Yahweh, the god of the heavens¦217111, has¦217107 given me all these earthly¦217106 kingdoms¦217105, and he's given me the job of building¦217116 a house¦217119 for him¦217132 in Yerushalem¦217120, which¦217121 is in Yehudah¦217122. \add To help with that,\add* \add ≈anyone who's¦217123 from there is allowed to return, and may their god Yahweh be with them and help them\add*.\x + \xo 36:23: \xt Isa 44:28.\x*
